{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games","id":1547828,"title":"Ascension in games","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-01-19T06:14:53-08:00","id":1547828,"title":"Ascension in games","content":"I'd like to know how ascension affects your games and players actions, if it ever do. <br /> I have some issues with ascension as written in M20 for a few reasons:<br /> <br /> 1) Ascension is described as a very, very rare state (&quot;more of an ideal than an accomplishment&quot; M20 p.23) by which mages often disagree what it means. So, mages aren't sure what it is nor how to achieve it. Why would a mage seek something that he doesn't know if its real and you dont know what is/how to seek? Why would one actively seek/want Ascension?<br /> <br /> 2) If there is no objective Ascension, every mage might ascend differently and there is no definition of what Ascension really *is*. The books gives examples like jesus and Buddha, but also people who ascended through aggressiveness and negative doings. So, how does one knows that he has truly ascended? And would other mages acknowledge that? What if he thinks he ascended but didn't? <br /> <br /> 3)My main issue: M20 describes ascension in p.370 as<br /> <br /> &quot;As The Book of Mirrors points out (pps. 60-61), Ascension is not hitting Arete 10 or maxing out all your Spheres. It\u2019s not about power but about the transcendence of the need for power. Mere power, in Mage, is a trap. The more a mage pursues it, the further she gets from ultimate Ascension. Even if her Path is all about power (see the Might is Right paradigm in Chapter Ten), that person must still grow beyond the need to acquire power.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Since ascension depends on paradigm *and isn't strictly related to higher/good moral and virtue*, why does seeking power gets in the way of ascending? Why could one ascend by going on a killing spree but not seeking power?<br /> More so, if ascension is directly related to magickal knowledge (stated in raw), why increasing Arete/Spheres would be bad for ascending?<br /> <br /> In conclusion, players are always seeking more xp, power, Arete, etc. How can you play the game *and* seek ascension when growing in power is bad for ascension?<br /> How do you reconcile the seek of power that every game has and ascension?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-19T21:30:56-08:00","id":1547841,"title":"","content":"In fact, Ascension is a very elusibe concept in Mage. In someways one could say the same about <i>Golconda</i>, but imo it's even more complicated (and at least <i>Golconda</i> has in theory a systematic advantage, where AFAIK Ascension does not have one). When they say it's about the &quot;transcendence of the need for power&quot;, one might be inclined to think that it's a more psychological state of being, would that be like &quot;being satisfied&quot; with what one already knows? Is it like &quot;escaping the cycle of desire&quot;, in a Schopenhauerian sense? So many questions...I'm going to stay tuned to this discussion here, perhaps we can help each other find enlightment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-20T18:09:44-08:00","id":1547865,"title":"","content":"Concepts like Ascension, Transcendence, and to some degree Golconda seem to fill a certain ideological or thematic space in their associated lines. It seems as though they're intended to provide some manner of perspective, suggesting that there is something more beyond &quot;this,&quot; whatever &quot;this&quot; happens to be in relation to any individual character or the world setting in general. They're concepts which are deliberately left wide open to personal interpretation because they wouldn't otherwise serve the narrative role they do.<br /> <br /> In our Mage games, characters sometimes muse and speculate over the possibility, role or goal of Ascension, but it's hasn't ever been treated as a personal driving goal so much as a convenient explanation for certain unusual trends and convergences of events (some of which have come about in surprising or eerie ways which had nothing to do with any planning on the part of myself or the players.) If I were ever to treat Ascension as a more blatant game factor, it would probably be used as a way for a character or setting to retire gracefully from play. Even within a couple chronicles spanning well over a decade, we've not had a character who's come close to becoming an Oracle (which is sometimes presented as the state of a Mage who's approached personal Ascension but put off the final step to remain involved in things,) and only one character who's been offered archmastery but chosen not to accept for the time being. (He feels he has an obligation to remain in a more traditional mentor role for the latest generation of Scientists, at least until things become more stable within the Tradition.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28664,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger","user":"Steve Bridger","date":". 01-21-2025, 06:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger","name":"Steve Bridger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-20T18:13:58-08:00","id":1547866,"title":"","content":"Maybe it's my love for old Dr. Strange comics, but I always thought of it as figuring out how to transcend one's existence as an individual and become one with everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-20T20:54:40-08:00","id":1547868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1547841#post1547841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact, Ascension is a very elusibe concept in Mage. In someways one could say the same about <i>Golconda</i>, but imo it's even more complicated (and at least <i>Golconda</i> has in theory a systematic advantage, where AFAIK Ascension does not have one). When they say it's about the &quot;transcendence of the need for power&quot;, one might be inclined to think that it's a more psychological state of being, would that be like &quot;being satisfied&quot; with what one already knows? Is it like &quot;escaping the cycle of desire&quot;, in a Schopenhauerian sense? So many questions...I'm going to stay tuned to this discussion here, perhaps we can help each other find enlightment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that\u2019s because with Golconda you can achieve it and keep playing, whereas with Ascension you immediately become an NPC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-21T04:27:08-08:00","id":1547869,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12348_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12348\" data-vbnamecard=\"12348\">Herr Meister</a> , &quot;being satisfied&quot; with what one already know is\u2026very lame for a mage game. Players (and characters) should always try to get better. We all crave for more challenges, growth, xp and power. If ascending is to stop doing that, well, I dont see a reason to ascend.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26996_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26996\" data-vbnamecard=\"26996\">Amethyst</a> yes, that's a good point. Achieving ascension means that you turn into an NPC and is &quot;gone&quot;, maybe even from in-game reality.<br /> <br /> That is why ascension should play it's part with players trying to achieve it. And that just strengths my arguments of #3 issue in my OP.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28664\" data-vbnamecard=\"28664\">Steve Bridger</a>, I am more interested in the Path to ascension rather achieving ascension itself (for the reason Amethyst posted). For a game that has &quot;ascension&quot; in its name, I find the concept widely ignored in games. And I believe the reasons might be the ones I listed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-21T07:09:51-08:00","id":1547876,"title":"","content":"If we take the asumptions you mentioned then:<br /> hyper focus = ascension<br /> generalizing, expanding your mindset = higher arete<br /> In conclusion the more power you have the harder it is but the stronger you get when its done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-21T08:41:41-08:00","id":1547878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1547869#post1547869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[USER=&quot;12348&quot;]I am more interested in the Path to ascension rather achieving ascension itself (for the reason Amethyst posted). For a game that has &quot;ascension&quot; in its name, I find the concept widely ignored in games. And I believe the reasons might be the ones I listed?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mostly agree, but before exploring any criticism, I want to ponder of how Mage wants you to do this Ascencion thing. In my experience and from what I can gather from the books.<br /> <br /> Ascencion, much like Golconda, it's something a player may want to achieve for purely roleplaying reasons. It's not mandatory, but it IS part of the often forgotten underpinings of the game<br /> <br /> Seekings and the Avatar are the tools the game gives the ST to steer the players to their personal Ascencion. Because players will want to raise Arete, you can as ST craft a&quot; path of Ascencion&quot;, if that makes sense, and insinuate it to the character. There's no &quot;system&quot; for this (and I imagine this was intentional), but it's there as a narrative and you do have tools to make use of it if you want. This should be talked with the player, of course.<br /> <br /> Note that this being the case, Spheres have nothing to do with Ascencion, but Arete does.This isn't contradictory with the idea that reaching Arete 10 isn't Ascencion, you could say it merely means you're not getting any more &quot;clues&quot;, and you should already know by this point how to reach it (to support this idea, there's a whole Merit in MotA that implies some Archmasters at Arete 8-10 commit ritual suicide and reincarnation because they now have an idea of how to Ascend but also know they're not going to reach it in their current incarnation)<br /> <hr /><br /> I think it IS a contradiction to say that ascencion depends on Paradigm, then say that &quot;power it's a trap&quot;, when both things need to be defined within Paradigm in the first place. M20 falls into this contradiction because it wants to put all the focus on the ....well... Focus, and on this idea that &quot;everyone may be equally rigth&quot; ...<br /> <br /> ... but Mage's &quot;Ascencion&quot; was never <i>subjective </i>to begin with. Ascencion may be an empty variable, and the books may toy with the idea that it doesn't exist, but as I see it they're very much consistent in how they treat &quot;Ascended&quot; <i>as a concept</i>:<br /> <br /> *There's no such thing as &quot;Ascended mage characters&quot; (the Oracles are explicitly not part of the Ascended. Still they're the closest to Ascencion. Exemplars and mages that reached Godhood aren't considered Ascended, and are implied to be further from it).<br /> <br /> Thus, it's more likely that Ascencion doesn't exist than Ascencion being a state one can reach and remain being a &quot;character&quot; at all, even as an NPC.<br /> <br /> *I'm pretty sure (but unfortunately I don't remember where this happened) that there was, once, in a Mage fiction, a character that was implied to <i>maybe</i> having Ascended. It was said that mage in question vanished, and no magick could be used to assert what happened to her - as if she was erased from existence alltogether.<br /> <br /> SO:<br /> <br /> Ascencion it's a state where the mage vanishes from Reality(tm) and becomes unreachable to any kind of magick. What happens to the mage it's a mistery, as much as what happens to Wraiths that Transcend. <br /> <br /> It's a very &quot;orientalist&quot; concept, which should be no wonder since the game has a strong inspiration in orientalist beliefs - it also makes sense with the Gnostic underpinings of WoD, where the goal could be to &quot;escape&quot; the prission of the Demiurge into a higher state of being.<br /> <br /> When you think about Ascencion this way, the reason of why &quot;power it's a trap&quot; it's evident: <b>Power it's </b><b>wordly </b>(it works &quot;on the world&quot;, and on yourself as part of it). If the idea it's to transcend the world in it's entirely, being more cappable doesn't do much. It gives you less reason to want to escape, and helps you forming more ties with the world as you can affect and mold more of it. It doesn't make you &quot;unable&quot; to ascend (well, except maybe for Archspheres in MotA, but that's an outlier), it just steers you on the opposite direction<br /> <hr /><br /> Mage of any edition past 1rst and early 2nd wants &quot;Paradigm/Focus&quot; to be the key that structures everything in the game, with everyone being &quot;possibly right&quot;. But, as they say, &quot;one thing it's what you want, and another what you get&quot;<br /> <br /> I feel like mage often struggles between 1ed ideas of &quot;reality it's a lie, the truth it's magick&quot; - where you could say that the Technocracy it's very much wrong, and Focus it's a clutch for noobs at magick, and the Ascencion it's to transcend reality - and latter editions that try to be more open and vage about the true nature of the world<br /> <br /> It's like when Mage says the Spheres don't exist in game, or are just a belief system or a commmon language of the Traditions, and not the real structure of magick ... while giving no tools of how magick could be structured depending on Paradigm ... Granted, Mage does have *some* optional tools (mostly in older editions) to make Spheres more of a function of Paradigm: (technocratic spheres, minnor spheres and the DA system.). <br /> <br /> I think if MtA wants to make Ascencion an ideal for players to strive foward, while retaining the concept of Focus as the core of the game, it needs some guidelines to &quot;build Ascencion&quot; from the structure of your Focus (If I'm allowed to be heretical: prefferably with actual rules and advantages to it). And also incorporate and balance the idea of Focuses that <i>don't have</i> Ascencion\u200b as a goal, that don't focus on any sort of trascendence or extintion whatsoever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-21T09:07:51-08:00","id":1547879,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28439\" data-vbnamecard=\"28439\">quelsec</a> could you explain better whst you mean, please? Hyper focus = ascension?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> , first, amazing post, tyvm<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Note that this being the case, Spheres have nothing to do with Ascencion, but Arete does.This isn't contradictory with the idea that reaching Arete 10 isn't Ascencion, you could say it merely means you're not getting any more &quot;clues&quot;, and you should already know by this point how to reach it (to support this idea, there's a whole Merit in MotA that implies some Archmasters at Arete 8-10 commit ritual suicide and reincarnation because they now have an idea of how to Ascend but also know they're not going to reach it in their current incarnation) </div> </div> </div>Indeed. If M20 just said that Arete 10\u2260 ascension, I'd be ok with it. The issue is that they say that more Arete gets in the way of ascension. But i see you covered that later in your post.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think it IS a contradiction to say that ascencion depends on Paradigm, then say that &quot;power it's a trap&quot;, when both things need to be defined within Paradigm in the first place. M20 falls into this contradiction because it wants to put all the focus on the ....well... Focus, and on this idea that &quot;everyone may be equally rigth&quot; ... </div> </div> </div>It's even worse. It says it depends on paradigm and there are several ways to ascend EXCEPT getting power (even if your paradigm is &quot;Might is Right&quot;, they literally specify that at p.370.<br /> <br /> To me, it seems they want to portray ascending as a higher virtue, like those monks that are above the regular mortals because they are not attached to material things and greedy stuff (such as power) and are thus, superior.<br /> <br /> But then, they also have examples of mages that adcended in agreassive and mean ways. So\u2026 another contradiction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> *I'm pretty sure (but unfortunately I don't remember where this happened) that there was, once, in a Mage fiction, a character that was implied to maybe having Ascended. It was said that mage in question vanished, and no magick could be used to assert what happened to her - as if she was erased from existence alltogether </div> </div> </div>I believe there is something about that in M20, have to look for it later.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When you think about Ascencion this way, the reason of why &quot;power it's a trap&quot; it's evident: Power it's wordly (it works &quot;on the world&quot;, and on yourself as part of it). If the idea it's to transcend the world in it's entirely, being more cappable doesn't do much. It gives you less reason to want to escape, and helps you forming more ties with the world as you can affect and mold more of it. It doesn't make you &quot;unable&quot; to ascend (well, except maybe for Archspheres in MotA, but that's an outlier), it just steers you on the opposite direction </div> </div> </div>Here you made a very good point. Power do form ties with the world. And so does making friends. Or lovers. Or eating. Or anything that brings pleasure and joy and emotions. There is an infinite number of things that might attach you to the world, power isn't the only nor the strongest one. Yet, M20 makes it so it's the only thing, so I can't agree with your line of thought.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also, would love to see some arguments about my issues in OP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-21T09:40:08-08:00","id":1547880,"title":"","content":"There are two reasons that I think Ascension is regularly sidelined. The first is that it is much harder to define what it is. Golconda is clearly some kind of balance between states, and Transcendence has to do with resolution, but Ascension involves some kind of mostly undefined enlightenment and escape, often based in pop-psychology/pop-religion enlightenment. It's seems like a niche goal for a few paradigms rather than an actual metaphysical element of the world.<br /> <br /> The second, though, is that it pushes against the game itself. It doesn't fit into the plot of most chronicles. Indeed, it often suggests that worldly conflicts are a distraction from Personal Ascension. That's true mechanically, as personal power, spheres, and even (strangely) Arete are said to be traps that interfere with Ascension (Masters of the Art says this, I believe).<br /> <br /> Contrast this with Transcendence. Thematically, it ties in with many ghost stories, unfinished business, and passing on. It is intensely personal for each Wraith and ties into character themes, passions, and fetters- things that exist whether the character is pursuing Transcendence or not. Also, many of the factions in Wraith are actively against Transcendence, so pursuing it doesn't sideline the rest of the setting, it engages it.<br /> <br /> What's the fix? Well, I'd reframe the quest for Ascension. While achieving it does mean completely transcending the world as the mage knows it, this can't be achieved by actively rejecting the world. Instead, the key to achieving Ascension lies within the world. I'd steal a page from Promethean. There's a lot of overlap between the quest for Ascension and Promethean's quest for humanity. Both involve the characters trying to learn about something they cannot fully comprehend.<br /> <br /> So I'd steal the touchstone system from Promethean and use that to track progress towards Ascension. The steps towards it and rooted in the character's actions with respect to the world and to the other people in it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-21T23:44:02-08:00","id":1547888,"title":"","content":"They're actually <i>is</i> a book in the <b>\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bMage</b> line that takes a stab at defining what Ascension is: <b>Masters of the Art</b>, one of the last books of the second edition. Note, however, that it was written back when people were still taking it as a given that Ascension meant letting go of what we now call Focus. <br /> <br /> The thing that's constantly repeated is that it isn't about power; it's about &quot;broad understanding&quot;. Terms like &quot;broad perspective&quot; and &quot;holistic&quot; are tossed around. Archmasters are criticized for getting stuck in &quot;one way of thinking&quot;. <br /> <div style=\"margin-left:40px\">The real trick of Ascension is that it isn't about magical power. It's really about who you are. Becoming a more holy, enlightened, spiritually pure person is the true goal of Ascension\u2026</div><br /> The final word in the book comes in a box talking about &quot;Ascension in the Context of Salvation&quot;. It talks a bit about Golconda, Transcendence, and &quot;even changelings have their own enlightened states through which they attain the one strength to take on the world.&quot; (As an aside, I notice that werewolves aren't included in this discussion. Strange.) It contrasts Ascension with these in that they involve accepting or balancing your dark side, whereas Ascension involves purifying it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-22T00:50:40-08:00","id":1547889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1547880#post1547880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'd steal the touchstone system from Promethean and use that to track progress towards Ascension. The steps towards it and rooted in the character's actions with respect to the world and to the other people in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>To that end, you might want to look at <a href=\"https://search.app/D9MJ2BVu4Jdp5ELd6\" target=\"_blank\">The Paradigm's Progress</a>. I'm not quite sold on it; I'd personally prefer a system that poses challenges to one's Paradigm, with the player having a &quot;fail laterally&quot; option where it's revealed that the character might need to change course in some way in order to advance further. But in terms of implementing something like Promethean's Milestone system, it's a good place to start.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-22T05:57:36-08:00","id":1547893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1547879#post1547879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28439\" data-vbnamecard=\"28439\">quelsec</a> could you explain better whst you mean, please? Hyper focus = ascension?<br /> <br /> <br /> ...........<br /> <br /> Also, would love to see some arguments about my issues in OP.</div> </div> </div> </div>I interpret it so Ascension requires you to dig deep in your own paradigm superstisions, Narrow the field.<br /> Increasing arete takes you closer to the &quot;universal meta magic theory&quot; (belief as magic). Therefore it directly interferes with you geting autistic on your paradigm to the point of transformation.<br /> <br /> So in short to &quot;Ascend&quot; you have to master what you know and believe. But the wider is the range of your paradigm (higher arete) the harder it is to do it.<br /> In my private cosmology Every splat part from demons started as a mage that ascended.<br /> <br /> As to how it works in the game. Here you should understand that i consider things like changing to a fae, vampire, werewolf, lich even and so on... all as minor ascenisons.<br /> So if you have an impatient character that considers ascension as gaining knowledge and imortality then its lichdom for him. Vampirism is another way of easy ascension, But the more Arete you have, the mor options open for you. You may find your ideal as a spirit, shapechanger, fae, or ,if you managed to master your paradigm at a high enough Arete, a god.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-22T10:07:17-08:00","id":1547894,"title":"","content":"Well, Ascencion comes in the long line of trascendence, golconda and similar higher-states that other splats of WoD mention.<br /> <br /> It is as such, an overcoming of the material, like a gnostic or buddhist elevation. It relates to removing yourself from the afflictions, concerns, illusions and fears of the material world (which can in WoD be every realm a mage can reach). So it's more shedding all the weight of life and reality, without losing your lucidity or falling to abandon. It's becoming weightless, able to absorb everything without being defined or afflicted by anything. Like a sainthood, able to act upon the world without being acted against.<br /> <br /> All and all, I do think that having higher Arete is important, for the Spheres give the mage a more hollistic and deep understanding of the world, and all the gears, bonds and networks that works it. But it does not give Ascencion by itself. It also means that you overcome your own mundane Paradigm, shedding that too. That limits, that narrows the vision of a mage. All is Truth or All can be Truth for an Ascended mage. <br /> <br /> But, according to most accounts of Ascencion in the setting, I believe one transcends to another dimension once they Ascend. So... I don't know if a mage can reach ascencion and still act in the world. If so, Ascencion would indeed be very selfish, just a turning off from all wordly concerns. If Jesus and Buddha are the example, then the Ascencion should be a state not of absolute power nor omniscience, but one that frees the mage from hinderings of spiritual and mental nature, they are of free spirit and mind, capable of understanding others and the world around them with great clarity, in the hopes of helping such a world reach a similar state. Like a benign virus spreading.<br /> <br /> <br /> Maybe being unclouded, unhindered, and unbound to your most essential core are the true definitions of Ascencion, and all else is just rethorics. If so, then yeah, you can be an evil Ascended who does not do evil things because you are defined by them, or feel compulsed to (like an ambition to become a millionaire no matter the costs, which could be germinated by years of propaganda and great men spiel), but just because that is your simple and deliberate wish.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-22T14:19:50-08:00","id":1547898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1547893#post1547893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I interpret it so Ascension requires you to dig deep in your own paradigm superstisions, Narrow the field.<br /> Increasing arete takes you closer to the &quot;universal meta magic theory&quot; (belief as magic). Therefore it directly interferes with you geting autistic on your paradigm to the point of transformation.<br /> <br /> So in short to &quot;Ascend&quot; you have to master what you know and believe. But the wider is the range of your paradigm (higher arete) the harder it is to do it.<br /> In my private cosmology Every splat part from demons started as a mage that ascended.<br /> <br /> As to how it works in the game. Here you should understand that i consider things like changing to a fae, vampire, werewolf, lich even and so on... all as minor ascenisons.<br /> So if you have an impatient character that considers ascension as gaining knowledge and imortality then its lichdom for him. Vampirism is another way of easy ascension, But the more Arete you have, the mor options open for you. You may find your ideal as a spirit, shapechanger, fae, or ,if you managed to master your paradigm at a high enough Arete, a god.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is pretty much the opposite of the published interpretation of Ascension. It is, in fact, a description of the trap that Archmasters fall into. Oracles (the guys who actually made it to Ascension, then stopped right at the final step) side themselves from Archmasters in that they broaden the field, rather than narrow it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-22T16:11:32-08:00","id":1547901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1547898#post1547898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is pretty much the opposite of the published interpretation of Ascension. It is, in fact, a description of the trap that Archmasters fall into. Oracles (the guys who actually made it to Ascension, then stopped right at the final step) side themselves from Archmasters in that they broaden the field, rather than narrow it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mistake the mastery of the known paradigm with sphere mastery. One is practical the other one phylosophical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-27T05:05:19-08:00","id":1547973,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25534_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25534\" data-vbnamecard=\"25534\">Banu_Saulot</a> Sometimes ascension is described as the classic transcendence: free yourself from selfish thoughts and materialism/greed.<br /> <br /> But then they say that ascension is a personal thing that depends on your paradigm, so it isn't necessarily the classic one? In theory one could ascend by means of violence and aggressiveness. <br /> <br /> The only paradigm that can't ascend is Might is Right, because fuck this paradigm, you shouldn't seek power.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28439\" data-vbnamecard=\"28439\">quelsec</a> Why do you say that higher Arete gives you a wider range of your paradigm?<br /> Arete shouldnt change paradigm. It gives you a better understanding on how reality and magick works *inside your paradigm*.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-27T06:38:02-08:00","id":1547975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1547973#post1547973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28439\" data-vbnamecard=\"28439\">quelsec</a> Why do you say that higher Arete gives you a wider range of your paradigm?<br /> Arete shouldnt change paradigm. It gives you a better understanding on how reality and magick works *inside your paradigm*.</div> </div> </div> </div>My understanding is that a better understanding of the paradigm is practically a different but similar paradigm in itself. When my players advance in arete they must learn something first and that something changes the way they see magic. That often changes when they cant do magic and how they interpret it making it a wholy new paradigm, a wider one.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-27T21:23:31-08:00","id":1547993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1547901#post1547901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mistake the mastery of the known paradigm with sphere mastery. One is practical the other one phylosophical.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mastery of the known paradigm is what defines an Archmaster; Sphere mastery is what defines an Exemplar. Ascension is achieved by moving beyond any one paradigm; at least, according to <b>Masters of the Art</b> in particular, and earlier editions of <b>Mage</b> in general. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1547973#post1547973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25534_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25534\" data-vbnamecard=\"25534\">Banu_Saulot</a> Sometimes ascension is described as the classic transcendence: free yourself from selfish thoughts and materialism/greed.<br /> <br /> But then they say that ascension is a personal thing that depends on your paradigm, so it isn't necessarily the classic one? In theory one could ascend by means of violence and aggressiveness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, certainly; different mages use different paths to reach Ascension. But if the older material has any validity, all of those Paths eventually broaden as the mage pushes beyond her paradigm's limits. If it always works within your paradigm, that's only because your paradigm gets redefined in increasingly broad terms. But it's also valid to view the final stages of the Path to Ascension as developing a flexibility of thought, an open-mindedness if you will, that lets you go <i>beyond</i> your paradigm. It's what growing beyond the tools is about<b></b>: the gradual realization that your Magick comes from within, and that the instruments of your practice are merely aids to be used or discarded as you see fit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-28T03:10:48-08:00","id":1547995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1547975#post1547975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My understanding is that a better understanding of the paradigm is practically a different but similar paradigm in itself. When my players advance in arete they must learn something first and that something changes the way they see magic. That often changes when they cant do magic and how they interpret it making it a wholy new paradigm, a wider one.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You don't get a new paradigm when you increase Arete, you refine your paradigm, which doesn't necessarily mean a &quot;wider&quot; paradigm. Also, what do you mean by wider?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> You're describing what happens when you max Arete. I'm not sure this is what happens in Ascension.<br /> <br /> Anyway, how do you concile the fact that ascension seems to be &quot;against seeking power&quot; to the game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-28T05:17:20-08:00","id":1547998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1547995#post1547995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You don't get a new paradigm when you increase Arete, you refine your paradigm, which doesn't necessarily mean a &quot;wider&quot; paradigm. Also, what do you mean by wider?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> You're describing what happens when you max Arete. I'm not sure this is what happens in Ascension.<br /> <br /> Anyway, how do you concile the fact that ascension seems to be &quot;against seeking power&quot; to the game?</div> </div> </div> </div>If we assume that at arete 10 the mage knows its all willwork. Then its a progress from the basic starting paradigm and evolwing slowly twoards &quot;its all just willwork&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-28T09:20:33-08:00","id":1548002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1547998#post1547998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If we assume that at arete 10 the mage knows its all willwork. Then its a progress from the basic starting paradigm and evolwing slowly twoards &quot;its all just willwork&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That assumes two things.<br /> <br /> 1) It is all willwork.<br /> <br /> 2) At Arete 10 a mage knows this.<br /> <br /> I don't see a reason to assume either one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-28T10:29:24-08:00","id":1548003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1548002#post1548002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That assumes two things.<br /> <br /> 1) It is all willwork.<br /> <br /> 2) At Arete 10 a mage knows this.<br /> <br /> I don't see a reason to assume either one.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it is willwork, thats why every paradigm works. We know that as participants of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-28T11:04:48-08:00","id":1548004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1547998#post1547998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If we assume that at arete 10 the mage knows its all willwork. Then its a progress from the basic starting paradigm and evolwing slowly twoards &quot;its all just willwork&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, fair enough. So, to run through the argument again: gaining Arete means you climb the stair of knowing it's all willwork, and this broadens the paradigm instead of focusing on it. And to achieve ascension one should delve into it, which means that getting more Arete is not the way to ascension and in fact could get in the way, as M20 says. <br /> <br /> Ok, I can accept that explanation. However, I still would like to know, then, how would you fit ascension in a game and why would a mage seek it?<br /> <br /> From an ooc perspective, it's also part of the game to seek and achieve power, increase spheres, Arete, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-28T12:05:38-08:00","id":1548006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1548003#post1548003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But it is willwork, thats why every paradigm works. We know that as participants of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>We know there are deeper truths behind the paradigms that mages see more of as they rise in Arete, and there is the indication that many paradigms tend to be pointing to the same truths. We don't know that that deeper truth is that all magic is pure willworking with no deeper metaphysical truth. That's an extrapolation by parts of the player base.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that even the idea of Will as a core component of magic only works if we stretch the meaning of Will quite a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-28T14:13:38-08:00","id":1548009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1548006#post1548006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We know there are deeper truths behind the paradigms that mages see more of as they rise in Arete, and there is the indication that many paradigms tend to be pointing to the same truths. We don't know that that deeper truth is that all magic is pure willworking with no deeper metaphysical truth. That's an extrapolation by parts of the player base.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that even the idea of Will as a core component of magic only works if we stretch the meaning of Will quite a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure its fuzzy in the details but notice that the more arete a mage has the less tools he needs. Ending with 0 at 10. That would imply that they were never needed in the firs place. From there we can asume that if we have no tools we need no practice if we need no practice we need no paradigm or THE paradigm is willwork.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/1548007-live-on-backerkit-trinity-continuum-steam-wars#post1548007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, I can accept that explanation. However, I still would like to know, then, how would you fit ascension in a game and why would a mage seek it?<br /> <br /> From an ooc perspective, it's also part of the game to seek and achieve power, increase spheres, Arete, etc.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Take note this is my personal take<br /> <br /> Ascension is a way to become immortal it also defines the ideal of ones paradigm. To seek ascension is to really want to become one with your paradigm like buddists do. If youre impatient and do that on arete 4-5 you did not quite made it becoming a lich, vampire, spirit of modest power. Arete 6-8 ascension would be on the level of totemic spirits. 10 Would be gods.<br /> <br /> So why would a mage want ascension? Its the core of ones belief. It also gives immortality and some more power. You are free of paradox.<br /> <br /> How would i make it part of the game? As character motivations, especialy NPCs. Ascension in itself reminds me of budda and the looking for hell in demon the descent.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-29T03:57:07-08:00","id":1548020,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> now and then this subject pops in this forum. M20 makes it clear that mages are all doing the same thing and it is all willworking.<br /> <br /> Sure, in-game it's a bit more complex, with paradigm and etc, but at the bottom, yeah it's willworking.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1548009#post1548009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take note this is my personal take<br /> <br /> Ascension is a way to become immortal it also defines the ideal of ones paradigm. To seek ascension is to really want to become one with your paradigm like buddists do. If youre impatient and do that on arete 4-5 you did not quite made it becoming a lich, vampire, spirit of modest power. Arete 6-8 ascension would be on the level of totemic spirits. 10 Would be gods.<br /> <br /> So why would a mage want ascension? Its the core of ones belief. It also gives immortality and some more power. You are free of paradox.<br /> <br /> How would i make it part of the game? As character motivations, especialy NPCs. Ascension in itself reminds me of budda and the looking for hell in demon the descent.</div> </div> </div> </div>This goes against what is written in the books, though. Arete is not related to ascension. Nor immortality (not necessarily). We are not sure ascension gives more power or makes you free of paradox. Probably not, because: 1) you can't achieve ascension by seeking power and 2) after ascending is said that you leave this Reality, so things like Paradox doesn't matter anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-29T07:00:38-08:00","id":1548025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1548009#post1548009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure its fuzzy in the details but notice that the more arete a mage has the less tools he needs. Ending with 0 at 10. That would imply that they were never needed in the firs place. From there we can asume that if we have no tools we need no practice if we need no practice we need no paradigm or THE paradigm is willwork.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I used to argue this a long time ago, but that's taking a game mechanic and turning it into an in game metaphysic. It also leads to some strange consequences, like mages abandoning their beliefs and morals as they rise in Arete.<br /> <br /> Also, there's a common trope in fantasy and sci-fi about the characters getting so good at their at their skills they no longer need the same rigid steps they used to. Sometimes this is them growing beyond their previous paradigm, but often this is just because the steps were just crutches to make magic easier or easier to understand.<br /> <br /> And this is the direction M20 took. Mages aren't abandoning foci, they are internalizing them. The oracle stops needing drugs to get into an altered mental state not because he doesn't get into an altered mental state, but because he doesn't need to use drugs to get there anymore. The martial artist doesn't need complicated forms to direct the chi flow in his body because he can do that directly, but his paradigm is still based around chi flow.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1548020#post1548020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> now and then this subject pops in this forum. M20 makes it clear that mages are all doing the same thing and it is all willworking.<br /> <br /> Sure, in-game it's a bit more complex, with paradigm and etc, but at the bottom, yeah it's willworking.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Everyone doing the same thing, yes, but as you say, in game what that same thing is is much more complicated. Willpower is certainly a part of the process, but that's not what most mages mean when they talk about mystical Will (if they even talk about mystical Will).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-29T07:07:50-08:00","id":1548026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1548025#post1548025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And this is the direction M20 took. Mages aren't abandoning foci, they are internalizing them. The oracle stops needing drugs to get into an altered mental state not because he doesn't get into an altered mental state, but because he doesn't need to use drugs to get there anymore. The martial artist doesn't need complicated forms to direct the chi flow in his body because he can do that directly, but his paradigm is still based around chi flow.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah this loses all sense when we have a son of ether with a plasma or lightninig gun, how would he internalize that? My theory makes way more sense.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-29T07:13:05-08:00","id":1548027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1548020#post1548020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[USER=&quot;758&quot;]<br /> This goes against what is written in the books, though. Arete is not related to ascension. Nor immortality (not necessarily). We are not sure ascension gives more power or makes you free of paradox. Probably not, because: 1) you can't achieve ascension by seeking power and 2) after ascending is said that you leave this Reality, so things like Paradox doesn't matter anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>As i said its my take on it.<br /> 1) You do not have to seek power to gain power. Perhaps its a power you cant gain by seeking power.<br /> 2) Leaving reality is in line with becoming a spirit/god. A good example are Majin incana from malephas. Thats a perfect example of ascendence for me.<br /> Aditionally spirits dont get paradox so turning to a spirit still fits my theory.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-29T10:46:13-08:00","id":1548030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1548026#post1548026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah this loses all sense when we have a son of ether with a plasma or lightninig gun, how would he internalize that?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why SoE can't drop foci until higher Arete, and why Technocrats <i>never</i> drop their foci, no matter how high Arete gets. So there are clear examples of mages who do not drop their paradigm even at high Arete.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-29T13:40:07-08:00","id":1548033,"title":"","content":"I find Mage Ascencion's concepts fun for literature, but for a game Awakening works so much better. Seeking the Mysteries of the world in search of Gnosis, discovering what there is and what there can be. Reaching for access of the Supernal, which is a form of Ascencion in itself. <br /> <br /> The Paths also build a more mystical mage rather than the comic book spread of Traditions, which have a lot of problems other than that.<br /> <br /> Besides, Ascencion lack of a morality system like Wisdom or Humanity also weakens a bit of the experience. You could say that Ascencion would be Humanity or Wisdom 9-10 coupled with a search for a higher state of surpassing worries and needs. Only Arete does not offer enough resources for representing that climbing. <br /> <br /> I don't think I've ever heard of a Mage Ascencion game with focus in Ascencion. Just like if I've heard of a single Golconda game in Vampire it was already one too many.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-30T07:10:19-08:00","id":1548051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1548025#post1548025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I used to argue this a long time ago, but that's taking a game mechanic and turning it into an in game metaphysic. It also leads to some strange consequences, like mages abandoning their beliefs and morals as they rise in Arete.</div> </div> </div> </div>IMHO, this is one of the areas where M20's more nuanced take is immensely helpful. In earlier editions, there wasn't much clarity as to what &quot;paradigm&quot; referred to: it was assumed to be a mixture of how you think the world works and how you go about working Effects. M20's Focus rules give you Paradigms that define how you think the world works, and Practices that define how you go about working Effects. In this context, a Path to Ascension arguably says nothing about abandoning one's Paradigm (e.g., Might make Right or Everything is Data); but it arguably <i>does</i> still at least imply that following the Path to Ascension involves overcoming the need for your Practices. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1548025#post1548025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, there's a common trope in fantasy and sci-fi about the characters getting so good at their at their skills they no longer need the same rigid steps they used to. Sometimes this is them growing beyond their previous paradigm, but often this is just because the steps were just crutches to make magic easier or easier to understand.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026and that's essentially the same as transcending your Practices. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1548025#post1548025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And this is the direction M20 took. Mages aren't abandoning foci, they are internalizing them. The oracle stops needing drugs to get into an altered mental state not because he doesn't get into an altered mental state, but because he doesn't need to use drugs to get there anymore. The martial artist doesn't need complicated forms to direct the chi flow in his body because he can do that directly, but his paradigm is still based around chi flow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it, though? Chi flow (or, more generally, Energy; M20 p.591) is an Instrument that the Martial Artist uses in his Practice. When he surpasses the need to use that Instrument, is his Focus <i>really</i> still based around chi flow? <br /> <br /> When the Martial Artist no longer needs to use <i>any</i> of his Instruments, is he <i>really</i> still Practicing Martial Arts? Or has he moved beyond his Practice to sheer Willworking? Granted, he retains access to those Instruments if he wants to use them; but the issue is that he no longer <i>needs</i> to. <br /> <br /> Also: I've never said that raising Arete to 10 is what Ascension is. The books <i>do</i> seem to indicate that increasing Arete is <i>helpful</i>, though. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-30T07:14:35-08:00","id":1548053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1548030#post1548030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's why SoE can't drop foci until higher Arete, and why Technocrats <i>never</i> drop their foci, no matter how high Arete gets. So there are clear examples of mages who do not drop their paradigm even at high Arete.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. And to the best of my knowledge, nobody has said otherwise. Indeed, I've flat out quoted material that says that Archmasters <i>don't</i> &quot;drop their paradigm&quot; even at high Arete \u2014 and that <i>that's why they can't Ascend.</i> <br /> <br /> Ascension isn't made possible by <i>mastering</i> your Practices; it's made possible by <i>going beyond them</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-30-2025, 10:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-30T11:34:55-08:00","id":1548060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1548051#post1548051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IMHO, this is one of the areas where M20's more nuanced take is immensely helpful. In earlier editions, there wasn't much clarity as to what &quot;paradigm&quot; referred to: it was assumed to be a mixture of how you think the world works and how you go about working Effects. M20's Focus rules give you Paradigms that define how you think the world works, and Practices that define how you go about working Effects. In this context, a Path to Ascension arguably says nothing about abandoning one's Paradigm (e.g., Might make Right or Everything is Data); but it arguably <i>does</i> still at least imply that following the Path to Ascension involves overcoming the need for your Practices.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are helpful, though they keep blurring the lines, with Paradigms that could also be Practices and Practices that could also be Instruments (or vice versa). Really, how you think the world works is often split amont Paradigm and Practice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2026and that's essentially the same as transcending your Practices. </div> </div> </div>In specific cases, yes. Usually, though, the character is still using the same powers they were before, just with more understanding, or more freely, or at a higher level. That's unsurprising, since most stories don't have the kind of subjective metaphysics Mage does, so there isn't even the possibility that they are doing something different.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is it, though? Chi flow (or, more generally, Energy; M20 p.591) is an Instrument that the Martial Artist uses in his Practice. When he surpasses the need to use that Instrument, is his Focus <i>really</i> still based around chi flow? </div> </div> </div>I picked the example for illustrative purposes with the Katas as the instrument and the Chi as the Practice. So given that, yes it is.<br /> <br /> And even if he grows beyond all the instruments associated with the practice of chi manipulation, I would say it still is. While I think some mages may indeed grow beyond their practice, for most, their practice grows with them. A high Arete version of that mage will likely have a far deeper and more wider ranging idea of what chi manipulation is, certainly one that is different than his younger self did. That doesn't mean it is a different practice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or has he moved beyond his Practice to sheer Willworking? </div> </div> </div>That, I think, is the big leap. And the answer depends a lot on what is meant by Willworking, but if we go with the most straightforward - that a mage directly wills something and it happens with no intermediate steps- I don't think he has.<br /> <br /> And if we do include intermediate steps, if we tack a 'because' onto the end of 'and it happens,' well, the answer to your question is much more complicated.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-30T11:52:20-08:00","id":1548064,"title":"","content":"Iirc, in M20 you drop your instruments and practices, but not your paradigm. So, it still has a &quot;why&quot; thing works in the mage head (even though, ooc, we know it works because he believes). Still, it is probably close enough to willworking, since you doesn't need to use any practice nor instrument, to be called that.<br /> <br /> Also, idk why we are discussing that, since:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1548051#post1548051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also: I've never said that raising Arete to 10 is what Ascension is. The books <i>do</i> seem to indicate that increasing Arete is <i>helpful</i>, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, raising Arete does not help ascending. Quite the contrary, according to M20 pg.370 (which I quoted here in this thread), it gets in the way, because you cant achieve ascension while &quot;seeking power&quot;, even if your paradigm says so (Might is Right) and that's one of my issues with ascension as described.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-30T12:13:08-08:00","id":1548065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1548064#post1548064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Iirc, in M20 you drop your instruments and practices, but not your paradigm. So, it still has a &quot;why&quot; thing works in the mage head (even though, ooc, we know it works because he believes). Still, it is probably close enough to willworking, since you doesn't need to use any practice nor instrument, to be called that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Strictly speaking the section on Arete on pg 329 only mentions dropping Instruments, not Practice. Whether dropping all instruments also means dropping Practice is unclear. It could go either way.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-01T15:19:03-08:00","id":1548103,"title":"","content":"Also, raising your Arete isn't &quot;seeking power&quot;; and raising it <i>doesn\u2019t</i> automatically interfere with the Path to Ascension. A case could be made that raising Spheres above 5 is &quot;seeking power&quot; and locks you out of achieving Ascension; that latter part is certainly what <b>Masters of the Art</b> said, though it seems to conflate &quot;seeking power&quot; and &quot;rigidly adhering to your paradigm to the exclusion of all else&quot;. <br /> <br /> I think we need a more nuanced view of what a Paradigm is in order to speak sensibly about this. I would recommend Charles Siegel's <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/446015/prism-of-focus\" target=\"_blank\">Prism of Focus</a> for this, particularly his Tenets system, which provides structure to Paradigm. In particular, one of the Tenets listed there is Openness: to what extent does the mage's Paradigm allow for the possibility that other Paradigms might be true? This is an extension of the MRev notion that paradigms can be Open or Closed to varying degrees. This, and the notion that Paradigms aren't inherently set in stone: it's entirely possible <i>and</i><i> appropriate</i> for a mage's Paradigm to evolve over time. <br /> <br /> What I've been describing as &quot;growing beyond your paradigm&quot; is more properly described as &quot;evolving your Paradigm to be more Open&quot;. The material about what Ascension is strongly implies that in order to Ascend, you must evolve your Paradigm into an Open one: mages with Closed Paradigms cannot Ascend; and it's arguable that even Hierarchical Paradigms (&quot;your Focus is entirely valid; but my Focus is inherently better&quot;) would have difficulty with Ascension. Archmasters are blocked from Ascension because their Paradigm tends to become more Closed as they advance. <br /> <br /> You can develop your understanding of &quot;your Paradigm&quot; as much as you want; and I would argue that <i>that, </i>not &quot;pursuit of power&quot;, is what Arete models. It's why raising Arete involves Seekings which challenge the mage's worldview. But the reason why raising Arete isn't sufficient to Ascend is because Ascension demands Openness; and if your increases in Arete aren't resulting in your Paradigm becoming more Open, it's not moving you towards Ascension. This is another way of describing what I meant by &quot;broadening your paradigm&quot;: a broad Paradigm <i>is</i> an Open Paradigm, and vice versa. <br /> <br /> And yes, this means that Technocrats tend not to Ascend, because Technocratic Paradigms tend to be Closed. But then, Technocrats generally don't <i>pursue </i>Ascension. Neither do the Disparates, for that matter; the pursuit of Ascension (in a personal sense) is nearly always a Traditions thing. So it makes sense that Ascension is uniquely compatible with the Traditions' emphasis on Open Paradigms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-02T18:28:33-08:00","id":1548124,"title":"","content":"Problem with the whole arete/archmaster discussion is that the books, including m20 says fundamentally contradictory things.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200bThings were pretty consistent in 1st and 2nd edition. 1st had magical power and understanding correlated with proximity to ascension, with oracles being joined by archmages after they reached a certain level. <br /> <br /> 2nd didn't make the distinction either, with only mentions that you don't ascend juqt by reaching ar\u00eate 10, with the fiction character of the core book ascending during her death while clearly not being a master. <br /> <br /> The masters of the art came and introduced the whole thing. It didn't make sense then, it doesn't makes sense in m20 either. <br /> <br /> <br /> Why I say that? Because of avatars and how arete is increased. <br /> <br /> So avatar wants to lead their mages to ascension, that's one of, if the not the main characteristics of their &quot;personality&quot; given to us. In fact that's how they are differenciated with nephandic inverted avatar, who no longer seeks ascension, but descension (something book of the fallen messed up, but that's another thing). <br /> <br /> <br /> Now, how does a mage raise power to a achieve his potential pinacle? Raising arete, which requires going through a seeking. Seeking which is entirely in the hands of the avatar. <br /> <br /> So the avatar is what allow the mage to raise in arete, it is also explicity said that they tailor their challenges and soul searching \u00e9piphanie based on the mages paradigm. <br /> <br /> All that to help the mage walk toward ascension. <br /> <br /> And then we're told that this process.... Makes mages less likely to achieve ascension? <br /> <br /> <br /> I mean, really, archmaster should be more likely to achieve it, as higher seeking are said to be even more difficult and more life changing. <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-03T04:59:40-08:00","id":1548138,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> I believe you're talking about the Storyteller book from revised that describes open, closed, etc paradigms. Ok, why do you say that open paradigms have nore chance to ascend than closed ones? You have any source from the books for that claim? I can't remember reading anything of the sort.<br /> I'd disagree on that. I think any paradigm has equal chance of ascending.<br /> <br /> Also, if raising Arete and spheres isn't &quot;seeking power&quot;, then what is? I do understand that Arete is way more than mere power, it represents the mage's knowledge and understanding of Reality, and I'd agree it is a good ascension &quot;meter&quot;, but the books like to say otherwise.<br /> <br /> M20 p.370<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As The Book of Mirrors points out (pps. 60-61), Ascension is not hitting Arete 10 or maxing out all your Spheres. It\u2019s not about power but about the transcendence of the need for power. Mere power, in Mage, is a trap. The more a mage pursues it, the further she gets from ultimate Ascension. </div> </div> </div><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24043\" data-vbnamecard=\"24043\">Nyremne</a> I agree with everything you posted. I really can't understand why M20 makes ascension look like becoming a selfless, non materialistic, non power seeking monk, but then they say that ascending depends on paradigm, so it doesn't need to be that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-03T09:22:47-08:00","id":1548144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1548103#post1548103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think we need a more nuanced view of what a Paradigm is in order to speak sensibly about this. I would recommend Charles Siegel's <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/446015/prism-of-focus\" target=\"_blank\">Prism of Focus</a> for this, particularly his Tenets system, which provides structure to Paradigm. In particular, one of the Tenets listed there is Openness: to what extent does the mage's Paradigm allow for the possibility that other Paradigms might be true? This is an extension of the MRev notion that paradigms can be Open or Closed to varying degrees. This, and the notion that Paradigms aren't inherently set in stone: it's entirely possible <i>and</i><i> appropriate</i> for a mage's Paradigm to evolve over time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this largely resolves earlier conflicts between 'abandoning practice' and 'deepening practice.' I'd add that it would make sense that Openness come in at least two dimensions. There's openness to the possibility that other Paradigms (and Practices for that matter) might be valid, and there's openness to adjusting your own viewpoint. That is, does a mage stretch his own paradigm and practices to fit new wisdom and enlightenment, or does he shoehorn that new understanding into his existing paradigm so that he has to change as little as possible.<br /> <br /> This may seem like splitting hairs as the two are not independent ideas, but I don't think acceptance of other mages' paradigms means that much for Ascension if it doesn't come along with an openness of viewpoint. The latter, I think, has more to do with Ascension.<br /> <br /> I also suspect Openness is a quality that is conducive to Ascension rather than a requirement for Ascension itself. After all, it appears that sometimes Ascension is achieved suddenly and without preparation much like Awakenings often are.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-03T10:45:22-08:00","id":1548146,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24043\" data-vbnamecard=\"24043\">Nyremne</a>'s approach appears to be &quot;Masters of the Art doesn't make sense to me, so I'll disregard it and everything that follows from it, such as similar content in M20.&quot; And it's perfectly fine if you want to run your Chronicles that way. I'm trying a different approach: can I <i>make sense </i>\u200bof <b>Masters of the Art</b>? If so, that validates an existing published book instead of tossing it, and it opens up more possibilities for how the game can be played. With this in mind: <br /> <br /> 1. Raising Arete is helpful for Ascension. It's not necessary to get to Arete 10 in order to Ascend, and you might not be able to Ascend even if you get to Arete 10; but the higher your Arete, the more likely you'll be able to Ascend. <br /> <br /> 2. Raising Spheres can be helpful, harmful, or neutral to the Path of Ascension. Unlike Arete, which is a measure of how attuned you are to whatever Ascension is, Spheres are all about <i>what you can do. </i>That doesn't automatically make them a trap; but it <i>does</i> mean that a mage that focuses too much on them has fallen into the trap of power. <b>Masters of the Art</b> describes Exemplars as mages who become overly focused on the Spheres and block their Path to Ascension in the process. This works reasonably well as is; all that's needed is something to indicate that the mage has developed an unhealthy fascination with the Spheres, and is no longer seeing them as a means to an end but as an end in and of themselves. <br /> <br /> 3. Focus can also be either helpful or harmful to the Path of Ascension. <b>Masters of the Art</b> talks about &quot;growing beyond your paradigm&quot;; and it claims that Archmasters have become so focused on a single paradigm that they've blocked their Path to Ascension. Being a transitional book between 2e and Revised, it doesn't actually have M20's concept of a Focus composed of a Paradigm, Practices, and Instruments; it just has a paradigm, and the foci that let you actualize it. (Well, technically each Tradition provides a Philosophy and either a Style or Theories and Practices depending o on the edition, which are roughly analogous to Paradigm and Practice; but they're joined at the hip, meaning that each Style or Practice flows from one Philosophy and the two are extremely easy to conflate.) So the concept needs some refinement for use with Revised and M20. Since I'm referring to both M20 and earlier editions, I'm going to capitalize Focus, Paradigm, and Practice when referring to M20's concepts, and I'll use lowercase paradigm, practices, and foci to refer to the concepts in the earlier editions. <br /> <br /> In the Revised edition, <b>Bitter Road</b> introduces the Paradigm Styles: Rigid, Closed, Open, and Liberal. <b>Guide to the Traditions</b> builds on that, introducing notions such as how deep your grasp on your paradigm is (Surface, Shallow, Strong, or Deep), what Spheres the mage prefers to use, and how the Avatar's Essence influences the paradigm. It then has a section on Altering Paradigm, noting that paradigm can evolve over time, not just becoming deeper but also shifting it. This is where you see the notion that a paradigm can have both depth and openness, and that the two don't necessarily align. <br /> <br /> I think this distinction between Surface/Shallow/Strong/Deep and Rigid/Closed/Open/Liberal is key to understanding why we're taking part each other. 1e and 2e conflated these, saying that as your Arete increases you get both a deeper understanding of your paradigm and a broader understanding of <i>other people's </i>paradigms. MRev and M20 don't exactly abandon this, but don't really embrace it either. This is where I think Lord Revan is coming from: he sees Arete as being a measure of how deep your understanding of your paradigm is; so the idea that raising Arete broadens your horizons feels wrong. Nyremne sees Arete as being about broadening your horizons; so the idea that Arete 10 isn't the same as Ascension feels wrong. <br /> <br /> Openness <i>does</i> seem to match the 1e and 2e notion of &quot;growing beyond your paradigm&quot; reasonably well, in the sense that the more open-minded you are with respect to others' paradigms, the more it makes sense that you'd be able to adopt their practices for your own use. Your own paradigm gradually ceases to be the be-all and end-all of how magic works and becomes just one model among many that are at your disposal. Where 1e and 2e assume that everyone develops this naturally as Arete increases, MRev allows for more options: that's where &quot;Archmasters are stuck in their paradigm&quot; comes in, with the idea being that the more they fixate on their own way of doing things, the more Closed and then Rigid their paradigms become; and that their fixation on their own paradigm is what prevents them from being able to Ascend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-03T10:49:06-08:00","id":1548147,"title":"","content":"I seem to remember that Masters of the Art also said pursuing Arete was a barrier to Ascension too. My book is in storage, though, so I can't check.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-03T10:57:14-08:00","id":1548148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1548144#post1548144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think this largely resolves earlier conflicts between 'abandoning practice' and 'deepening practice.' I'd add that it would make sense that Openness come in at least two dimensions. There's openness to the possibility that other Paradigms (and Practices for that matter) might be valid, and there's openness to adjusting your own viewpoint. That is, does a mage stretch his own paradigm and practices to fit new wisdom and enlightenment, or does he shoehorn that new understanding into his existing paradigm so that he has to change as little as possible.<br /> <br /> This may seem like splitting hairs as the two are not independent ideas, but I don't think acceptance of other mages' paradigms means that much for Ascension if it doesn't come along with an openness of viewpoint. The latter, I think, has more to do with Ascension.<br /> <br /> I also suspect Openness is a quality that is conducive to Ascension rather than a requirement for Ascension itself. After all, it appears that sometimes Ascension is achieved suddenly and without preparation much like Awakenings often are.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to view that last part as a bit like a Promethean achieving the New Dawn: if I were to systematize the process of Ascension, it would involve an Arete roll made during a Seeking, so that it <i>can</i> be achieved without reaching Arete 10; and things like &quot;is my Paradigm sufficiently Open?&quot; would either be a prerequisite to be able to make the roll at all or it would be a modifier of some sort. I <i>wouldn't</i> systematize the process, mind you; it should be left to Storyteller and player discretion. But these are the sorts of issues I'd ask the Storyteller to consider.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-03T11:12:28-08:00","id":1548149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1548147#post1548147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I seem to remember that Masters of the Art also said pursuing Arete was a barrier to Ascension too. My book is in storage, though, so I can't check.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me load it into my pdf reader, and see what its AI has to say: <br /> <br /> &quot;Arete does not interfere with Ascension. It is a measure of a mage's magical power and skill, with Archmages beginning with an Arete of six. However, it is important to note that an Archmage should not have a Sphere rating above six, and Storyteller approval is needed before raising Arete.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's possible that that's an AI Hallucination; I've seen them before. In other words, I might be wrong. But I don't think so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-03T12:22:08-08:00","id":1548150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1548146#post1548146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24043\" data-vbnamecard=\"24043\">Nyremne</a>'s approach appears to be &quot;Masters of the Art doesn't make sense to me, so I'll disregard it and everything that follows from it, such as similar content in M20.&quot; And it's perfectly fine if you want to run your Chronicles that way. I'm trying a different approach: can I <i>make sense </i>of <b>Masters of the Art</b>? If so, that validates an existing published book instead of tossing it, and it opens up more possibilities for how the game can be played. With this in mind:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 3. Focus can also be either helpful or harmful to the Path of Ascension. <b>Masters of the Art</b> talks about &quot;growing beyond your paradigm&quot;; and it claims that Archmasters have become so focused on a single paradigm that they've blocked their Path to Ascension. Being a transitional book between 2e and Revised, it doesn't actually have M20's concept of a Focus composed of a Paradigm, Practices, and Instruments; it just has a paradigm, and the foci that let you actualize it. (Well, technically each Tradition provides a Philosophy and either a Style or Theories and Practices depending o on the edition, which are roughly analogous to Paradigm and Practice; but they're joined at the hip, meaning that each Style or Practice flows from one Philosophy and the two are extremely easy to conflate.) So the concept needs some refinement for use with Revised and M20. Since I'm referring to both M20 and earlier editions, I'm going to capitalize Focus, Paradigm, and Practice when referring to M20's concepts, and I'll use lowercase paradigm, practices, and foci to refer to the concepts in the earlier editions.<br /> .<br /> <br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's not so much that I disregard it because Masters the the art made no sense to me, but that it repeatedly contradict itself. <br /> <br /> On the matter of arch masters VS ascension, we're both told that arch masters become so focused on their paradigms that they narrow their views and therefore close themselves to ascension. But the rest of the text tells us that arch masters grow closer to what we might refer as the purple paradigm, hence rejecting pure dogma in favor of a generalised meta understanding of magic. <br /> <br /> Which was one of the thing people didn't liked about it, that mages basically grew , out of their paradigms with higher arete, since, as you correctly pointed out, mage then didn't separated much if at all between practices and tools. So a high arete archmasters, unless technocrat, is a pure will worker with a purple paradigm. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-03T12:36:45-08:00","id":1548151,"title":"","content":"Honestly a simple way to keep that dynamic while making it all makes sense is to utterly disregard the idea that power or paradigm obsessions hinder the road to ascension.<br /> <br /> After all, if it was the case, avatars would make escaping that obsession a requirement of high level seeking.<br /> <br /> Plus, M20 made that boat sail away with the idea that even marauders can ascend.<br /> <br /> <br /> A way to explain why high arete don't simply ascend is simply their goals.<br /> <br /> Now, depending on their paradigm and own path, a mages ascension might be characterized by a form of letting goor on the contrary by something specific to achieve.<br /> <br /> Mage going the first way might, willingly or not, postpone their ascension because of attachment or personnal objectives. After all, ascended beings are no longer &quot;there&quot;, so a mage may want to let ascension be for another day.<br /> <br /> An exemple for that would be Senex, if he were to ascend, who would oppose voormas? Who would keep the watch over the entropy shard realm? Who would find dark souls to help return to their dharma?<br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> On the other end, a mage's path to ascension may be lengthened by the sheer difficulty of what the mage's try to accomplish.<br /> <br /> Hermes Trimegistus had to achieve total mastery of magic according to hermetic tradition. A son of ether or any other analytic mage may need to form a model of existence able to explain every possible phenomenom in existence without flaw or try to achieve a fundamental change to the world, making their ascension dependant on an epic, and therefore extremely hard to achieve goal.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That would resolve the paradox. Our arete 10 chorister postpone her ascension because she's wants to make sure her traditions, horizon realm and family will be safe without her. And our enlightenment 10 void engineer might only ascend if he succeed in making humanity a stable multi planetary species.<br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24043,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","user":"Nyremne","date":". 02-03-2025, 03:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-03T13:57:44-08:00","id":1548153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1548151#post1548151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly a simple way to keep that dynamic while making it all makes sense is to utterly disregard the idea that power or paradigm obsessions hinder the road to ascension.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that that's exactly the part that I'm trying <i>not</i> to utterly disregard. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1548151#post1548151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus, M20 made that boat sail away with the idea that even marauders can ascend.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yes\u2026 And? Marauders can develop open Paradigms, too, though it's harder for them; their thing is the ability to reject Consensual Reality and substitute one of their choosing. In my hypothetical systemized process of Ascension, being in Quiet would penalize the attempt to Ascend, but wouldn't block it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1548151#post1548151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, depending on their paradigm and own path, a mages ascension might be characterized by a form of letting go or on the contrary by something specific to achieve.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly. I'm glad to see an acknowledgement that something to the effect of the older editions' &quot;letting go&quot; approach is still valid; an awful lot of the talk here seemed to be saying that as of M20, the only way to Ascend is to zoom in on your Focus. Something strongly implied by the idea that the nature of Ascension is defined by your Paradigm. Because if the nature of Ascension is defined by your Paradigm, how is it possible for letting go of your paradigm to be a Path to Ascension? <br /> <br /> In that regard, my thinking is that, like so many other things in Mage, the nature of Ascension is <i>informed by </i>your Paradigm; but it isn't <i>defined </i>by it. There are some objective truths the we can state about Ascension, such as the fact that Ascending results in you leaving Reality as we know it, but not in the same way that a high-Quiet mage falls out of reality. There are details where different Paradigms interpret aspects of Ascension differently; but it shouldn't be so open that Ascension can be whatever you want it to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-03T16:06:33-08:00","id":1548162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1548153#post1548153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that that's exactly the part that I'm trying <i>not</i> to utterly disregard.<br /> <br /> <br /> Well, yes\u2026 And? Marauders can develop open Paradigms, too, though it's harder for them; their thing is the ability to reject Consensual Reality and substitute one of their choosing. In my hypothetical systemized process of Ascension, being in Quiet would penalize the attempt to Ascend, but wouldn't block it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Possibly. I'm glad to see an acknowledgement that something to the effect of the older editions' &quot;letting go&quot; approach is still valid; an awful lot of the talk here seemed to be saying that as of M20, the only way to Ascend is to zoom in on your Focus. Something strongly implied by the idea that the nature of Ascension is defined by your Paradigm. Because if the nature of Ascension is defined by your Paradigm, how is it possible for letting go of your paradigm to be a Path to Ascension?<br /> <br /> In that regard, my thinking is that, like so many other things in Mage, the nature of Ascension is <i>informed by </i>your Paradigm; but it isn't <i>defined </i>by it. There are some objective truths the we can state about Ascension, such as the fact that Ascending results in you leaving Reality as we know it, but not in the same way that a high-Quiet mage falls out of reality. There are details where different Paradigms interpret aspects of Ascension differently; but it shouldn't be so open that Ascension can be whatever you want it to be.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My comment for the marauder is about the context in which their ability to ascend is mentioned.<br /> <br /> The text centers the rise of quiet and to the point where reality itself kicks off the marauder.<br /> <br /> Which is the most closed paradigm thing one could be, rejecting reality so thoroughly that it utterly rejects you.<br /> <br /> That form of ascension shows that we can't assume an open paradigm is required.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the letting go part. I don't think it's really the position of old editions. The farther places I can find it is in revised, and most specifically, master of the art.<br /> <br /> 1st edition doesn't include it, and 2nd, which has, in my opinion, the best way to describe the whole thing and it's implementation in game, is extremely open on the ways to achieve it:<br /> <br /> &quot;Self-perfection is the common Holy Grail. Through it, a mystick becomes one with some greater entity or expands to full human potential to become more than merely flesh. Some posit that such Ascension is not a goal but an ongoing process. The answer, again, is up to you.<br /> <br /> Seekings and Arete play a large part in personal Ascension, but they only reflect in abstract terms what most mages spend lifetimes trying to achieve. The real test of personal Ascension comes through roleplaying \u2014 facing tests and triumphing while becoming one with your Art. A character who spends most of her experience on Arete and most of her time achieving some balance and perfection will Ascend more quickly than one who perfects his power with the Spheres.<br /> <br /> Some \u201ccommon\u201d routes toward personal Ascension might include:<br /> <br /> Journeys into the Otherworlds which inspire a view of the totality and unity of creation;<br /> <br /> Strict adherence to some art, magick, philosophy or religion which teaches \u201cThe Way\u201d to a chosen goal;<br /> <br /> Death as a sacrifice for the greater good;<br /> <br /> Forging an all-unifying theory which takes all things into account and respects the miracle which is each separate thing combined;<br /> <br /> Realizing that any attempt to quantify creation is doomed to fail and harmonizing with what is rather than with what one thinks there should be.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-03T16:38:49-08:00","id":1548163,"title":"","content":"From that, we can get that the form of paradigm does not impead ascension, the &quot;strict adherence to some art, Magick, philosophy or religion which teaches&quot; the way&quot; &quot; part describe to a T the concept of closed paradigm.<br /> <br /> In fact, the only thing that stops a mage from ascending is the caul (well, until book of the fallen) <br /> <br /> <br /> So if it's not letting go, what is the common denominator? <br /> <br /> From reading these hint, and the rest of the text, it's seems to be about &quot;achieving&quot;. <br /> <br /> Achieving inner peace, achieving unity with god/the gods/the Machine, achieving a complete Theorical model of the tellurian, or on the contraryy, achieving acceptance that the tellurian can't be codified, etc<br /> <br /> <br /> The mage &quot;simply&quot; needs an instinct of perfect self accomplishment. And that can take countless form. In fact, every paradigm could hold many ways to achieve it. <br /> <br /> Which would explain why avatars adapt their seeking based on paradigms. <br /> <br /> After all, by pushing their mage toward the pinacle of their beliefs, they might ascend by achieve it's perfection, or achieving the perfect renunciation of it. <br /> <br /> <br /> So, to take m20 paradigm classifications<br /> <br /> If &quot;everything is Chaos&quot;, you achieved total harmony with tha lack of order of the cosmos, or you created a meaning so profound that it defied chaos itself. <br /> <br /> If &quot;it's all fine, have faith&quot;, you finished your theory of the tellurian that explains why suffering is here, and why in the end, it's all for a good reason<br /> <br /> If there's &quot;divine order, earthly chaos&quot;, you self perfected into a agent of divine perfection into the world. Or you embraced the imperfection of the world<br /> <br /> If &quot;the world is a stage&quot;, youembraced your role to perfection, or you broke away from it all. <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bSo Porthos could have ascended, if rather than obsess over what he himself considered meaningless politics, he'd had focused on achieving self mastery, or abandoned utterly the hermetic inner fights to embrace the cosmos. <br /> <br /> Although one can argue that he achieved ascension by giving his life to save everything he cared about, and the world at large. <br /> <br /> <br /> In the end, from an extradiegetic perspective, the act of ascension is not that hard to conceptualise. It's the ultimate conclusion of a character's path, to such a degree that they leave the stage. <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> So it's paradigm, plus goals, plus inner conflicts<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-04T06:54:18-08:00","id":1548186,"title":"","content":"For Divine Order, Earthly Chaos or Have Faith, I'd take inspiration from the end of St Thomas Aquinas' life. A lifetime of writing exhaustive treatises on theology and morality (ones that are still considered some of the most comprehensive to this day), and then a few months before the end of his life he received a vision of just how much deeper the reality of God goes. After that he never wrote again, saying all of his works seemed like &quot;so much straw.&quot; <br /> <br /> There's no indication that he repudiated his works or thought they led people astray. Instead it seems that he either felt that anything he could write would fall short of what he had seen or that he could not translate his understanding into words anyone else could follow him on. <br /> <br /> That latter possibility, by the way, is a good explanation for why mages who Ascend don't stick around. It's not that they are whisked away, it is that their new point of view just doesn't compress down into the world in a way anyone else can access.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-18T18:29:13-08:00","id":1548579,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24043\" data-vbnamecard=\"24043\">Nyremne</a> I liked your explanations. What would you say is ascension for &quot;might is right&quot; paradigm, though, since M20 made it clear that pursuing power isn't a way to ascend (even to that very paradigm, which I think is very dumb).<br /> <br /> How do you relate those explanation with &quot;not seeking power&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-18T19:23:10-08:00","id":1548580,"title":"","content":"Not the person you've asked, but I've been keeping an eye on this thread, and I have some thoughts on the matter.<br /> <br /> I think the mistake is acting like the &quot;Might is Right&quot; Paradigm, as written in M20, is synonymous with &quot;increasing your personal power.&quot; If you read the entry, &quot;Might is Right&quot; as a Paradigm concept is not just a matter of your personal strength, but rather a belief about the nature of strength and how it relates to the rest of reality. It's about Social Darwinism, the idea that strength, regardless of who holds it, gets to determine what is right, or what is true.<br /> <br /> I haven't read the stuff in MotA that talks about Archspheres getting in the way of Ascension, but the vibe that I get from the part you quoted from M20 is that it's criticizing the idea of reducing Ascension to just raising Spheres and Arete. And that applies to &quot;Might is Right&quot; just as much as any other Paradigm. In the case of someone who believes in &quot;Might is Right,&quot; increasing their own power is an obvious course of action, but if Ascension involves embracing and engaging with the philosophy of your Paradigm beliefs, then it's not enough on its own.<br /> <br /> Going back to the idea that &quot;Might is Right&quot; as a Paradigm is about Social Darwinism, it's not just about increasing your personal power, but demonstrating it, exercising it, proving it. A Mage could raise their Spheres and Arete by isolating themselves in their research and avoiding conflict, but that does not fit with the idea that &quot;Might is Right.&quot; If you want to become a paragon of that ideal, then you need to use that power, prove its supremacy. A &quot;Might is Right&quot; Mage would need to use their strength to establish dominion over their &quot;inferiors.&quot; They would need to seek out challenges and overcome them in order to prove their strength. And what about this disgusting fad of &quot;democracy&quot; that's spreading across the world like a cancer, pretending that weaklings deserve to have as much say in how the world is run as their betters?<br /> <br /> Believing in &quot;Might is Right&quot; can also lead to some philosophically challenging questions, like how you handle being confronted by someone who is indisputably more powerful than yourself. Do you submit to the authority that their power bestows upon them? If you refuse, then you either need to abandon the idea that power alone confers legitimacy, or you need to commit yourself to proving yourself the superior being in the long run, maybe even risking your life in your refusal to submit. You can study the Spheres and raise your Arete without necessarily engaging with those kinds of issues, but they come with the territory of truly believing that &quot;Might is Right.&quot; And confronting those issues, and finding resolution to them, is how a &quot;Might is Right&quot; Mage follows their path to Ascension; improving your magical abilities is an important start, but it can't be the entirety.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-19T00:08:07-08:00","id":1548581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1548579#post1548579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24043\" data-vbnamecard=\"24043\">Nyremne</a> I liked your explanations. What would you say is ascension for &quot;might is right&quot; paradigm, though, since M20 made it clear that pursuing power isn't a way to ascend (even to that very paradigm, which I think is very dumb).<br /> <br /> How do you relate those explanation with &quot;not seeking power&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> On that I would purely discard the M20 position. <br /> Basing ourselves on the idea that one way to ascension is &quot;strict adherence to some art, Magick, philosophy or religion&quot; one following that paradigm would have to gain some power to achieve it. <br /> <br /> I'd say a mage on the might is right road would ascend in ways including:<br /> <br /> -achieving a degree of power in such a way that no one but the mage can dictates his life. In sum, &quot;winning the game&quot; of power, if only for one pinacle like moment. <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b- using achieved power to topple a massively powerful individual/faction/concept in such a way that, by his might, the mage forced the world to follow his way<br /> <br /> -using achieved power to in definitively protect the people/group/ideas he cares about <br /> <br /> -after many seeking and potentially Mind effects, cutting away every form of weakness possible. <br /> <br /> -or becoming a pure moral shapeshifter. Always going on the side of the winner. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I don't necessarily means the mage have to max out ar\u00eate and sph\u00e8res, or that he need to become a walking metaphysical nuke, but he need to have a moment of &quot;I cannot be toppled&quot;. <br /> <br /> For exemple, we could have a mage who, in his view of might is right, see a world where powerful beings or forces shapes both events and minds, and seeks to achieve a state where only he decides his fate.<br /> <br /> Such a mage wouldn't necessarily try to be a god, but would seeks to find way to cut away the strings of his fate, to make himself unbondable by mind controlling magic, until he's utterly defined onyl by himself. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Let's say we have Miranda, a mage who believes in might in right. She have seen her fellow mages, both allies and enemies, use mind altering magic. She saw nightfolks place gras on people, or trap them in blood bond. She met umbrood goslings who delight in shaping the fates of mortal, and she saw the effect of fate with time and entropy magic. <br /> <br /> <br /> In fact, let's say she has the flaw dark fate, to add to this. For her, the quest for ascension will be one where she steal her fate from the universe and screams at it &quot;by my hands only&quot;. <br /> <br /> So she'll work on mind magic to shield herself, study the intricacy of prophecy to find the loops, travel to the umbra to try to trick powerful being into giving her protection from the meddling of destiny (of course tricking them or besting them, making a pact would be another bound). <br /> <br /> In game term, she'd try to find way to gain merits such as unbondable. <br /> <br /> She may even go as far as using life and mind magic to alter her genes and personality so that even heredity or learned behavior could no longer rule over her. <br /> <br /> Finally, in one last, risk it all journey, she goes to the shard realm of entropy, using it to cut away her fate. Not just her dark fate, but all of it. When she leave the realm she's unbound. No one will ever control her, her fate is her own, gods and demons are bound to avoid her, she eludes the eye of prophecy. As far as she know, she may be the only truly free being in existence. <br /> <br /> And in that moment of pure triumph, of victory over a reality that would have chained her, she ascend. <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-19T11:30:41-08:00","id":1548591,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25886\" data-vbnamecard=\"25886\">Kharnov</a>, thanks for your answer. I like the Darwin explanation a lot. <br /> About the interation with a more powerful mage/being, I'd say that the Might is Right mage would acknowledge that is in the presence of a superior being, but would not be submissive to it. <br /> <br /> Now, the thing you didn't noticed is that M20 (and not only MotA) says that, not only Arete/Sphere isn't equal to Ascension, but it gets in the way to ascension. What do you have to say about that M20 statement?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24043\" data-vbnamecard=\"24043\">Nyremne</a> Yes, the only way I can see isbto ignore that paragraph I quoted from M20.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure ascension would come from a single action. <br /> <br /> And what about ascension meaning that the mage ia no longer in Reality anymore?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-19T12:13:09-08:00","id":1548593,"title":"","content":"A fun theory is the earth incubator theory. Ascending means you become a god, therefore you leave your nest and do stuff with the other fully ascended gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-19T19:13:59-08:00","id":1548604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1548591#post1548591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24043\" data-vbnamecard=\"24043\">Nyremne</a> Yes, the only way I can see isbto ignore that paragraph I quoted from M20.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure ascension would come from a single action.<br /> <br /> And what about ascension meaning that the mage ia no longer in Reality anymore?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It seems one of he most common occurrence is that indeed, the mage found the metaphorical door at the end of the universe and got out of the tellurian as we know it, either escaping reality to another plane of existence. in fact that's the fate of the only character whose ascended existence we see in the 2nd edition corebook<br /> <br /> <br /> Now what does that mean is variable. A mage may utterly escape reality in a gnostic way, abandoning this one to do what ascended beings do. <br /> <br /> Or they could merge with god, with entities like the machine, they could achieve anharmony so great that they're basically a part of the cosmos. <br /> <br /> Or they're still here, in a way, but in a part of the tellurian thzt non ascended beings cannot see, like spirits watching across the gauntlet. <br /> <br /> Maybe some still live here, maybe they highjack vatars to guide mages. Maybe they wait at the end of all time for all the ascended beings to meet. Maybe they became like the Womick of verbena legends and are shaping existence far beyond the horizon. <br /> <br /> <br /> The common things seems to be that, like the singularities of a black hole, ascended beings are sort of behind some event horizon that either remove them from here, or hide their nature from most. <br /> <br /> <br /> And of course, since ascension is said to resolve paradoxes, it may be that an ascended being match every individual date listed above. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-19T21:34:51-08:00","id":1548606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1548591#post1548591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25886\" data-vbnamecard=\"25886\">Kharnov</a>, thanks for your answer. I like the Darwin explanation a lot.<br /> About the interation with a more powerful mage/being, I'd say that the Might is Right mage would acknowledge that is in the presence of a superior being, but would not be submissive to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, but why though? If by &quot;submissive&quot; you mean boot-licking and fawning behaviour, then sure. But if &quot;Might is Right,&quot; and someone else is mightier, on what grounds do you justify defying them? They have the power, they get to make the decisions, that's the meaning of the &quot;Might is Right&quot; Paradigm. I'm not saying there aren't acceptable reasons, but simply asserting a convenient answer without sufficient justification doesn't work, in my opinion. Again &quot;Might is Right&quot; is not just about the Mage's personal power, but about the larger relationship between Power, Reality, and Truth. It's more than just an excuse for egotism.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1548591#post1548591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, the thing you didn't noticed is that M20 (and not only MotA) says that, not only Arete/Sphere isn't equal to Ascension, but it gets in the way to ascension. What do you have to say about that M20 statement?</div> </div> </div> </div>I noticed, and I wasn't trying to ignore it, but I probably could have addressed it more directly. The TL;DR is that I interpret it somewhat differently.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>M20 Core Rulebook, p.370</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As <b>The Book of Mirrors</b> points out (pgs. 60-61), Ascension is not hitting Arete 10 or maxing out all your Spheres. It's not about power but about <i>the transcendence of the need for power.</i> <u>Mere</u> power, in <b>Mage</b>, is a trap. The more a Mage <u>pursues</u> it, the further she gets from ultimate Ascension. Even if her Path is all <i>about</i> power (see the <b>Might is Right</b> paradigm in <b>Chapter Ten</b>), that person must still <u>grow beyond the <i>need</i></u> to acquire power. And if that sounds paradoxical, you're right. There are reasons that Ascension is easy to talk about but difficult to achieve.</div> </div> </div> </div>(Underlining added for emphasis by me)<br /> <br /> When I read this paragraph, it doesn't seem to me that it is saying that increasing your Spheres and Arete will necessarily make it harder for you to Ascend. Rather, it's talking about a narrow-minded fixation on the accumulation of power that leads to you ignoring the deeper philosophical or spiritual questions that will help to achieve Ascension. This was the sort of thing that I was referring to when I talked about a &quot;Might is Right&quot; Mage who sits in their Sanctum studying the Spheres rather than going out and living the truth of their Paradigm.<br /> <br /> Once again, &quot;Might is Right&quot; =/= &quot;I must be the strongest,&quot; and I think that is what that line about needing to &quot;grow beyond the need to acquire power&quot; is talking about. You don't have the be the strongest to adhere to the principles of &quot;Might is Right,&quot; you simply have to accept that power controls reality. I don't think there's anything there that says that gaining power gets in the way of Ascension, so long as your accumulation of magical potency is a byproduct of you following your Path, as opposed to being your obsession. Power can be accumulated as a means, but it can't be the end unto itself.<br /> <br /> I am willing to concede that the way MotA links Archmastery with an inability to Ascend does lend some support to the idea that advancing even base Sphere knowledge could similarly be an impediment, but I don't consider that to be an irreconcilable problem. It may simply be that Archmastery is impossible to achieve without a level of obsession that ultimately hinders the ability to Ascend in a way that lesser Sphere knowledge doesn't, and you can't escape from the ties that it creates on your soul once you've made that knowledge a part of your being, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-20T05:19:49-08:00","id":1548612,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24043\" data-vbnamecard=\"24043\">Nyremne</a>, that makes sense. I had the impression that an ascended mage would not have access (or would want) to interact with Reality, but I think that is not a restriction. While some ascended might be completely out of Reality, I dont see why some could still be in touch with Earth.<br /> <br /> Also, where did you get that paradox thing? I can't remember that from M20.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25886\" data-vbnamecard=\"25886\">Kharnov</a><br /> <br /> Ok, you have convinced me. Although there is a bit of mental gymnastics, you could give a plausible explanation. I still have some questions, though:<br /> <br /> -Since there seems to be an infinity of ways to ascend, which depends on paradigm, why someone seeking power for power's sake (like your mage studying spheres example) can't ascend? Why can someone ascend by the most unexpected and crazy way (marauders) but not by seeking power? <br /> <br /> Also, how would you describe ascension for an Etherite with Mechanistic Cosmos focused on physics and electromagnetism?<br /> <br /> And a Hermetic with Everything is Chaos paradigm and Chaos Magick as practice?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-20T10:27:30-08:00","id":1548621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1548612#post1548612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[USER=&quot;24043&quot;]<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25886\" data-vbnamecard=\"25886\">Kharnov</a><br /> <br /> Ok, you have convinced me. Although there is a bit of mental gymnastics, you could give a plausible explanation. I still have some questions, though:<br /> <br /> -Since there seems to be an infinity of ways to ascend, which depends on paradigm, why someone seeking power for power's sake (like your mage studying spheres example) can't ascend? Why can someone ascend by the most unexpected and crazy way (marauders) but not by seeking power?<br /> <br /> Also, how would you describe ascension for an Etherite with Mechanistic Cosmos focused on physics and electromagnetism?<br /> <br /> And a Hermetic with Everything is Chaos paradigm and Chaos Magick as practice?</div> </div> </div> </div>So, the answer is that I see Ascension as requiring you to engage with philosophical or spiritual issues that are bigger than just yourself. It entails enlightenment not just about yourself, but about the wider &quot;Truth&quot; that the Mage believes in. A desire for personal power that does not engage with any bigger or deeper questions about the nature of reality is too narrow-minded and egotistical for the kind of transcendental awareness demanded by Ascension. I would probably reject any path to Ascension that fails to confront those kinds of Big Questions, not just paths focused on personal power.<br /> <br /> I haven't spent as much time considering technmantic paradigms, so I don't have a lot of ideas about a physics-oriented Etherite. But I imagine that their route to Ascension would probably be tied up in their efforts to create a satisfying &quot;Theory of Everything&quot; that fits with their concept of SCIENCE! And eventually, their understanding of the system reaches a point where they Ascend to either become a larger part of that system, or to observe it from a higher level than their (comparatively) mundane embodied existence can allow.<br /> <br /> I am glad that you asked me about Chaos Magic, however, because that happens to be one of my favourite Paradigms, and I've actually been reading up on it a bunch lately! A Chaote's path to Ascension would probably involve really embracing the infinite possibilities of Chaos, how existence can be understood and engaged with in countless ways, including paradoxical or contradictory ones. It would also entail an understanding of the mutability of the Ego and identity; like the universe, the Chaos Mage can be anything, rejecting any fixed notions of who they are or ought to be. I feel like the route a Chaos Mage would follow to achieve Ascension would probably include the &quot;Transcend Your Limits&quot; Paradigm listed in the Book of Secrets.<br /> <br /> Bringing it back to Sphere knowledge, each of those examples can be used to illustrate different ways that a Mage might develop their powers on the route to Ascension. With an Etherite who believes in a Mechanistic Cosmos, it would be pretty likely that their Sphere knowledge would be consistently increasing as they followed their path to Ascension, because the way they believe that their magic works is closely tied to their understanding of the way that the universe works, and their path to Ascension is closely tied to that increasing knowledge. But that would simply be an unintended consequence of their search for Truth, not the point of what they are doing.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, for the Chaote that I described, increasing Sphere knowledge might be useful in some respects, but their path is much more philosophical. The kind of understanding that they need to transcend their conceptual limitations and expand their awareness of the cosmos would not necessarily translate into knowledge of specific Spheres in the same way that the Etherite's quest for SCIENCE! would. A Chaos Mage with lower Spheres and Arete, but a deeper understanding of the principles that their Paradigm espouses, could be closer to achieving Ascension than one with higher Sphere knowledge that has failed to really pursue the greater Truth to be found within their metaphysical framework.<br /> <br /> All of this rambling has helped me think of a way to maybe sum it up. I see Sphere knowledge being related to questions of &quot;How?&quot; while Ascension is more like questions of &quot;Why?&quot; If you're too focused on the &quot;How?&quot; questions, without ever thinking about the deeper &quot;Why?&quot; questions, then you will never reach Ascension. But it's quite possible to find the answers to &quot;How?&quot; questions while you're trying to understand the &quot;Why?&quot; questions. Again, power comes as a byproduct, or merely a means, to a greater end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-20T18:13:49-08:00","id":1548645,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25886\" data-vbnamecard=\"25886\">Kharnov</a>, great answer, I also like chaos magick pretty much!<br /> <br /> <br /> But what if the mage paradigm includes seeking power as a way to reach a higher truth?<br /> <br /> About the chaote, I'm not sure adding another paradigm would make much sense. Also, I think belief as a tool would have a bigger part on ascension? What you think?<br /> <br /> <br /> I really like the &quot;How?&quot; and &quot;Why?&quot; examples. It makes sense and that is a good way to add ascension in a game even though players do seek power a lot, because one could always seek both &quot;How?&quot; and &quot;Why?&quot;. Tbh, I believe the majority of mages do, and I could not think why one would not\u2026","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-20T19:45:27-08:00","id":1548649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1548612#post1548612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24043\" data-vbnamecard=\"24043\">Nyremne</a>, <br /> <br /> Also, where did you get that paradox thing? I can't remember that from M20.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh you won't find it anywhere in M20, it's something that appeared regularly on the matter of ascension in books like the guide to the traditions of the revised tradition book of the sons of ether","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-20T19:50:04-08:00","id":1548650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1548645#post1548645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25886\" data-vbnamecard=\"25886\">Kharnov</a>, <br /> <br /> But what if the mage paradigm includes seeking power as a way to reach a higher truth?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You touch something pretty important. It seems inevitable that for a lot of paradigm, a certain degree of power is required. <br /> <br /> If I want to seek the nature of the tellurian in the deepest reach of the umbra, I'll need to at least have the sphere power required to go there. If I want to achieve an ideal of perfection of self on earth, i'll need a certain mastery of spheres like life and mind to shape myself toward that ideals. If I believe technology has all the answer and my path to ascension is to creates marvelous tech to resolves things, well, I need the sphere to create that. <br /> <br /> <br /> And that includes high arete, it will be hard to shape my psyche and my body to become an avatar of divine perfection on earth if I don't have the brute power to fuel tha great work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-20T22:40:46-08:00","id":1548655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1548645#post1548645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25886\" data-vbnamecard=\"25886\">Kharnov</a>, great answer, I also like chaos magick pretty much!<br /> <br /> <br /> But what if the mage paradigm includes seeking power as a way to reach a higher truth?</div> </div> </div> </div>So, I feel like I've already addressed this via a couple of angles:<br /> <br /> 1) We've discussed how &quot;Might is Right&quot; is about more than just the personal power of the Mage. Focusing only on your own personal strength, while ignoring the wider issues and deeper questions represents a failure to fully engage with the Paradigm, which I would consider an impediment to Ascension.<br /> <br /> 2) Like with the Etherite example I provided above, in cases where pursuing Sphere knowledge either comes as a byproduct of pursuing a higher Truth, or serves as a means to the end of pursuing a higher Truth, then I wouldn't consider that something which would interfere with the pursuit of Ascension.<br /> <br /> But if you don't feel like either of those explanations cover the Paradigm that you have in mind, then I have to ask what kind of Paradigm that is?<br /> <br /> You keep focusing on the idea of &quot;seeking power,&quot; the Means/&quot;How&quot;, without really trying to clarify what kind of higher Truth, the End/&quot;Why&quot;, that it would be used to pursue. It's a bit like the Underwear Gnomes from South Park:<br /> <br /> Step 1: Seek Power<br /> Step 2: ????<br /> Step 3: Ascension<br /> <br /> Looking at all of the examples of Paradigms provided in M20, I can't think of any where &quot;how do I get more power&quot; is the first and last question raised. &quot;Transcend Your Limits&quot; probably comes the closest, and that still comes with bigger issues than just personal power that need to be considered, but I don't have the Book of Secrets on hand right now to check the details. If I was a Mage Storyteller, and a player brought me a custom Paradigm that just consisted of &quot;I Want to be Stronger,&quot; then I would probably reject it. It's just a desire, not the sort of comprehensive worldview that a Paradigm is supposed to be.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1548645#post1548645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About the chaote, I'm not sure adding another paradigm would make much sense. Also, I think belief as a tool would have a bigger part on ascension? What you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not absolutely necessary, but it fits very well with what I imagine Ascension from the perspective of Chaos Magic would look like, based on what I've read by Austin Osman Spare, Peter J. Carroll, Phil Hine, etc.<br /> <br /> &quot;Belief is a tool&quot; is a perfect example of a &quot;How&quot;, not a &quot;Why&quot;; the word &quot;tool&quot; is right in there. It's a Means, and you need to figure out the End that it's aimed at before it has any value in the pursuit of Ascension, just like the Spheres.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1548645#post1548645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like the &quot;How?&quot; and &quot;Why?&quot; examples. It makes sense and that is a good way to add ascension in a game even though players do seek power a lot, because one could always seek both &quot;How?&quot; and &quot;Why?&quot;. Tbh, I believe the majority of mages do, and I could not think why one would not\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, you can seek both at the same time, but not every inquiry a Mage makes is going to give answers to both questions, so time spent on &quot;How&quot; questions isn't always going to translate into progress on answering the &quot;Why&quot; questions. Thus, too much time spent on pursuing the answers of &quot;How&quot; questions, like the Spheres, without taking the time to consider the &quot;Why&quot; questions of what kind of ideal the Mage hopes to achieve or embody, can be a distraction from the path of Ascension instead of a boon. A dead end, or trap, if you will.<br /> <br /> And &quot;Why&quot; questions are often harder to answer than &quot;How&quot; questions, especially when the subject is how the entire universe is supposed to work. &quot;How&quot; is engineering, a discipline with practical and measurable outcomes. &quot;Why&quot; is philosophy, that discipline that's infamous for not having managed to conclusively answer most of the significant questions that it has raised over the last several thousand years.<br /> <br /> But to provide one example, I've spent a fair amount of time reading about &quot;The Dief&quot; and &quot;the Pit Bosses,&quot; the Syndicate Construct in Vancouver mentioned at the end of &quot;Technocracy: Syndicate.&quot; I'm going off of memory, but of the three Syndics they provide information about, I think it would be generous to say that one of them seems to spend any time on the &quot;Why&quot; questions. For another example, remember that story of the Himalayan Wars where reincarnating Akashics and Chakravanti were constantly seeking vengeance against those who had slain them in previous incarnations? That sure doesn't sound like Mages keeping focused on spiritual enlightenment. Mages are still people, and not every one of them is particularly committed to pursuing deep philosophical issues, preferring to pursue more mundane motivations than the nebulous concept of Ascension.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-21T09:23:26-08:00","id":1548677,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24043\" data-vbnamecard=\"24043\">Nyremne</a>, I see. Then this paradox thing isn't something set on stone. Could you provide a page or a quote of what it says?<br /> <br /> About your second sest, yeah, I agree. But you didn't answer the question.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25886\" data-vbnamecard=\"25886\">Kharnov</a> Yes, I understand and agree with your two points.<br /> I don't have any specific paradigm in mind. But I guess you are right, maybe every paradigm will have something deeper than just &quot;seek power&quot;.<br /> <br /> However, I have to say that, for this same reason, &quot;seeking power&quot; will always come together with seeking a higher truth. The mage that sits on his lab or library, studying and practicing his spheres to increase them, is not only adding dots on the sheet. In game, he is developing his paradigm further, discovering misteries of Reality.<br /> So, I ask, what/how is in fact &quot;seeking power&quot; as written in M20 in a way that hinders ascension?<br /> <br /> I understand that mages do have small mortal goals that would not help on ascension, like infighting. But when it comes to increasing power (arete/spheres) I'm not sure one could do it without &quot;How&quot; AND &quot;Why&quot; together.<br /> <br /> <br /> About the chaote, yeah I had Phil and Peter in mind, as well as everything I read about rl chaos magick.<br /> magick.<br /> While I liked you previous chaote example of ascension, do you have one that is not centered in identity change? I could see a chaote ascending by comprehending fully how Reality is shaped by Will, and connecting all of his other paradigms (if that's the case) and practices in a way that their deeper truth is Will and belief.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-21T14:34:13-08:00","id":1548688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1548677#post1548677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25886\" data-vbnamecard=\"25886\">Kharnov</a> Yes, I understand and agree with your two points.<br /> I don't have any specific paradigm in mind. But I guess you are right, maybe every paradigm will have something deeper than just &quot;seek power&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, I invite you to show me an example of a Paradigm written in M20 that doesn't include more.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1548677#post1548677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, I have to say that, for this same reason, &quot;seeking power&quot; will always come together with seeking a higher truth.</div> </div> </div> </div>To quote a funny person quoting a funny person:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528373#post1528373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pEZgJyTzqPg\" data-code=\"pEZgJyTzqPg\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/pEZgJyTzqPg/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1548677#post1548677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The mage that sits on his lab or library, studying and practicing his spheres to increase them, is not only adding dots on the sheet. In game, he is developing his paradigm further, discovering misteries of Reality.<br /> So, I ask, what/how is in fact &quot;seeking power&quot; as written in M20 in a way that hinders ascension?<br /> <br /> I understand that mages do have small mortal goals that would not help on ascension, like infighting. But when it comes to increasing power (arete/spheres) I'm not sure one could do it without &quot;How&quot; AND &quot;Why&quot; together.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can provide two very clear examples of the &quot;How&quot; and &quot;Why&quot; not coming together, by looking at two of the most famous Archmages:<br /> <br /> Porthos and Voormas.<br /> <br /> And before you say &quot;But MotA!&quot;, let's assume either that a) the concept of Archspheres hindering Ascension is false, or b) that they lose their Archspheres, but still have mastery of multiple Spheres, and at least some ranks in all of them.<br /> <br /> These two are pinnacles of Sphere knowledge and magical power. And yet it's easy to see just by looking at them that they both have personal flaws that conflict with the philosophical ideals of their Paradigms. Porthos is wracked by guilt and self-loathing, clearly lacking the divine perfection that is considered the ultimate goal of the Hermetic path. Meanwhile, Voormas has mastered the magical powers associated with the Euthanatos/Chakravanti while <b>blatantly</b> rejecting the core of their spiritual beliefs, gripped by a pathological fear of the Good Death.<br /> <br /> In both cases, they have managed to master the <b>tools</b> of their Paradigm without understanding or embracing the <b>wisdom</b> contained within the associated philosophies. The &quot;How&quot; and &quot;Why&quot; of a Paradigm are not joined at the hip, and time and effort pursuing one will not necessarily translate into the other.<br /> <br /> To reference Star Wars: Episode 2, you need to appreciate the difference between <b>knowledge</b> and <b>wisdom</b>.<br /> <br /> For another example, consider the act of killing a person. We're also going to just stop talking about Paradigm loosely for a moment, and employ the terminology provided in M20: a Focus consists of Paradigm, Practice, and Instruments. The Practice, combined with knowledge of the Spheres, will tell you &quot;How&quot; to use Instruments kill a person. But the philosophical concepts found within the Paradigm will help you understand &quot;Why&quot; you should, or should not, kill a person. How does learning about &quot;How&quot; the Forces Sphere works tell you &quot;Why&quot; you should, or should not, light a person on fire?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1548677#post1548677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About the chaote, yeah I had Phil and Peter in mind, as well as everything I read about rl chaos magick.<br /> magick.<br /> While I liked you previous chaote example of ascension, do you have one that is not centered in identity change? I could see a chaote ascending by comprehending fully how Reality is shaped by Will, and connecting all of his other paradigms (if that's the case) and practices in a way that their deeper truth is Will and belief.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is his Will? What does he Believe?<br /> <br /> You're just describing a mastery of the Practice, the Tool that is Belief. It's still &quot;How&quot; rather than &quot;Why&quot;. It works for the Etherite because the Etherite believes that there is a Truth to discover and describe, but the fluid nature of reality espoused in the philosophies of Chaos Magic rejects the pursuit of such all-encompassing notions of &quot;Truth&quot;; &quot;Nothing is True, and Everything is Permitted.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think the problem you may be having is that you want Ascension to be value-neutral, and it's not. Ascension is about finding an ideal, a concept of perfection, and pursuing it, embodying it. It seems like the only perfection you want to really consider is Omnipotence. And it seems like what you like about Chaos Magic is that it does not necessarily require any kind of spiritual or ideological commitment to work; it's just power to be harnessed, which might be why the concept you seem most attached to is &quot;belief is a <b>tool</b>.&quot;<br /> <br /> To take a step back for a second, one of the first things that I thought when I started reading this thread is that part of the problem you're having is that you want a Watsonian solution to a fundamentally Doyleist problem. The reason why the writers in Mage are consistently pushing back against the idea of Ascension being tied up in Spheres and Arete is because it's supposed to be something spiritual and ineffable, and letting that be reduced to &quot;My Numbers Are Bigger Than Yours&quot; is, to a lot of people (including yours truly), an intensely boring and disappointing answer to a question that's supposed to be a grand cosmic mystery. Any in-game explanations or theories that you can come up with don't really matter because the decision is based around out-of-game considerations about what the designers think would make the game more fun and interesting.<br /> <br /> In my opinion, if you really want Omnipotence to be a form of perfection that a Mage can pursue as a path to Ascension, then you have to go all in on that. You want to get Archspheres and still be allowed to Ascend? Fine. You have to get EVERY Archsphere. If Omnipotence is your idea of perfection, then that's what Omnipotence looks like in Mage.<br /> <br /> <br /> P.S. Lazy edit, but throw a big &quot;In My Opinion&quot; in around any point where I state what Ascension *is* or *supposed to be*. I feel like my take is at least moderately supported by what I've read in M20 and a few other scattered places, but I haven't read everything Mage has ever put out on the subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":". 02-21-2025, 06:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-22T01:42:48-08:00","id":1548693,"title":"","content":"Just a few brief thoughts: <br /> <br /> First, MotA doesn't say that Archmasters are trapped by their pursuit of Archspheres; that's Exemplars. Archmasters are trapped by their pursuit of a single paradigm. Bear in mind that this was written during the transition from 2e to Revised, long before M20 came along with its clarification about the distinction between Paradigm and Practice. In terms of what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25886\" data-vbnamecard=\"25886\">Kharnov</a> is talking about, M20's Practices are the &quot;How&quot;, and its Paradigms are the &quot;Why&quot;.<br /> <br /> And the idea to take away from MotA is that Archmasters get trapped by focusing too heavily on their Practices. The business about &quot;once you develop Archspheres, Ascension is no longer possible&quot; would be downstream from that, with the idea being that Archspheres can only be accessed through a Practice, or by becoming an Exemplar. If you want to maintain the idea that Archmasters can't Ascend, the way to argue it is to say that they <i>have to </i>focus on the &quot;How&quot; to the detriment of the &quot;Why&quot; in order to access the upper reaches of what the Spheres can do. <br /> <br /> On the subject of Marauders Ascending: I categorically reject the notion that a Marauder falling so far into Quiet that they completely disassociate from reality and fall out of it bears anything more than a surface level resemblance to Ascension. If Marauders can Ascend, they do so <i>despite </i>their Quiet, not <i>because of it. </i><br /> <br /> Ditto with Nephandic &quot;Ascension&quot;, but moreso: in MotA terms, Nephandi don't seek Ascensioon; they seek apotheosis, or they seek Oblivion. But actual Ascension? Becoming a god is a distraction from that. And Oblivion is arguably the polar opposite of Ascension. <br /> <br /> Finally, I think that one of the things that defines the Traditions is that each of them attempts to provide a vision of personal Ascension for their members to pursue. This is as opposed to the Technocracy and the Crafts: I'm not saying that a Black Hat or a Sister of Hypollyta can't Ascend; but for the most part, they do so without much help from their Convention or Craft. But one of the reasons the Traditions <i>exist </i>is to help their members Ascend; and in that regard, it would be interesting to walk through the Traditions and get a sense of what each one's vision of Ascension <i>is</i>. <br /> <br /> For example, the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Kitab_al-Alacir\" target=\"_blank\">Book of Ether</a> speaks of the Walls of Troy, a metaphor for reality. In this metaphor, everything is possible, even contradictory things. The Walls of Troy contain those things that have been accepted as possible, with everything outside the Walls being considered impossible. In this view, Ascension consists of tearing down the walls so that the Scientist truly accepts the infinite possibilities of reality. That's how an Etherite views Ascension: developing such a profound understanding of Ether Science that all things become possible. <br /> <br /> This is where the Revised Tradition Books come in handy. In particular, I would look at each one's take on the Tenth Sphere to get a sense of what sorts of concepts that Tradition would use in formulating its vision of Ascension.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-22T08:25:28-08:00","id":1548705,"title":"","content":"Thanks, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a>. As I've mentioned, I'm going off of second-hand information when it comes to MotA, so I appreciate the clarifications <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-22T11:59:26-08:00","id":1548710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1548688#post1548688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again, I invite you to show me an example of a Paradigm written in M20 that doesn't include more.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is none. I agreed with you.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I can provide two very clear examples of the &quot;How&quot; and &quot;Why&quot; not coming together, by looking at two of the most famous Archmages:<br /> <br /> Porthos and Voormas. </div> </div> </div>Well, the issue I see here is that we do not know thoae characters paradigm and you are just assuming they have the vanilla hermetic and euthanatos paradigm, which is too shallow and might not be true. <br /> Other big issue is that those chars were created long before M20, so paradigm had not the structure M20 provides.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> And before you say &quot;But MotA!&quot;, let's assume either that a) the concept of Archspheres hindering Ascension is false, or b) that they lose their Archspheres, but still have mastery of multiple Spheres, and at least some ranks in all of them. </div> </div> </div>I personally prefer to completely ignore MotA, because it is a 2e book AND the focus structure completely changed in M20. Also, there are no archspheres in M20 too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In both cases, they have managed to master the <b>tools</b> of their Paradigm without understanding or embracing the <b>wisdom</b> contained within the associated philosophies. The &quot;How&quot; and &quot;Why&quot; of a Paradigm are not joined at the hip, and time and effort pursuing one will not necessarily translate into the other. </div> </div> </div>I don't know enough about those characters to analyze their paradigm, in fact, I'm not sure their ever explained their paradigms in detail. If they did, please tell me where.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For another example, consider the act of killing a person. We're also going to just stop talking about Paradigm loosely for a moment, and employ the terminology provided in M20: a Focus consists of Paradigm, Practice, and Instruments. The Practice, combined with knowledge of the Spheres, will tell you &quot;How&quot; to use Instruments kill a person. But the philosophical concepts found within the Paradigm will help you understand &quot;Why&quot; you should, or should not, kill a person. How does learning about &quot;How&quot; the Forces Sphere works tell you &quot;Why&quot; you should, or should not, light a person on fire? </div> </div> </div>Tbh, the &quot;Why&quot; isn't why you should do something (kill someone or do magick), but &quot;why&quot; can you do it. Paradigms (as in M20) should explain why mage can alter Reality and not &quot;why&quot; they should. And the &quot;why can&quot; will (and have to) be very well on par with the &quot;how&quot;.<br /> <br /> A chaote could answer those questions (in a very, VERY, simplified answer) like that:<br /> <br /> \u2022 How can you change reality? By achieving an altered state of consciousness that allows you to send your Will into the universe <br /> <br /> \u2022 Why can you change reality? &quot;As above, so below&quot;. What happena in the macroscomic level is reflected in the microcosmic level. There is a connection between the universe &quot;mind&quot; and the human mind, meaning that when on an altered state of consciousness (gnosis), the mage can directly &quot;connect&quot; to reality and change it.<br /> <br /> By practicing and studying more about gnosis and how magick works, the mage would also understand better about the connection with the universe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What is his Will? What does he Believe?<br /> <br /> You're just describing a mastery of the Practice, the Tool that is Belief. It's still &quot;How&quot; rather than &quot;Why&quot;. It works for the Etherite because the Etherite believes that there is a Truth to discover and describe, but the fluid nature of reality espoused in the philosophies of Chaos Magic rejects the pursuit of such all-encompassing notions of &quot;Truth&quot;; &quot;Nothing is True, and Everything is Permitted.&quot; </div> </div> </div>It seems you are talking about open and closed paradigms? I believe chaos magick could be any of those. &quot;Everything is permitted&quot; could mean that you have no limits on your magick, but not that all paradigms are correct.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think the problem you may be having is that you want Ascension to be value-neutral, and it's not. Ascension is about finding an ideal, a concept of perfection, and pursuing it, embodying it. It seems like the only perfection you want to really consider is Omnipotence. And it seems like what you like about Chaos Magic is that it does not necessarily require any kind of spiritual or ideological commitment to work; it's just power to be harnessed, which might be why the concept you seem most attached to is &quot;belief is a <b>tool</b>.&quot; </div> </div> </div>Not at all. I wouldn't consider omnipotence ascension. I was just wondering why one wouldn't ascend if seeking to increase spheres and arete. This thread has helped me understand a lot.<br /> <br /> I just think they should have explained a lot better in M20 instead of just saying increase in arete/spheres is bad for ascension.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-22T14:41:37-08:00","id":1548711,"title":"","content":"To my taste, Ascension is a distraction and a trap. A character can get so focused on some ideal, impossible or otherwise, and it leads them down the wrong path.<br /> <br /> In one of the Star Wars animated shows, a Jedi character gets obsessed with the idea of force visions and destined heroes saving the galaxy. The resolution of that plotline is essentially that it is an understandable yet foolish distraction from the personal story being told, the story of him and his band of rebel friends, and the planet they want to liberate.<br /> <br /> Whatever the Storyteller's opinion of Ascension is, my OOC opinion, and the baseline most of my characters would tend to have IC unless I want them to seem like they're deeply influenced by propaganda (e.g. a Hermetic who has been raised in the order), is that it is meaningless and irrelevant. The absolute enlightenment of an individual means nothing without justice, and justice is interpersonal, it is worldly. Seek wisdom, but seek it as a means to guide your decision-making on worldly matters, to guide those of others, and to temper draws towards injustice and abuse of power.<br /> <br /> Basically, in a MTA game I'm more interested in saving the city from an oppressive reality zone than I am in Ascension, in WTA I'm more interested in saving an ecosystem from total destruction than I am in reaching Summer Country (or whatever 'win condition' you can think of), in VTM I'm more interested in unravelling the Primogen's plot than I am in Golconda, and so on.<br /> <br /> CTD is interesting because Siochain is a playable and plot-relevant state of being. A Siochain is not only compatible with a typical party, albeit one years into a chronicle, it's arguably an outright enhancement. What does it mean for a party if one of the PCs bears the Mantle of The Rogue With A Heart Of Gold, that they've become a supernatural being who truly sums up and IS the concept which weaves itself through millions of stories throughout human history? What does it mean for the plot if the PCs help a Thallain to stop being a Thallain, and instead become a Siochain, by taking up the Mantle of The Redeemed Villain or The Antihero? More to the point, reaching the state of Siochain involves the other PCs by default, since to get there you have to go through narrative arcs with a number of different characters.<br /> <br /> Basically unless I'm playing C20, I don't care about my PC 'ascending' as it were, and I would actively encourage my ST and fellow players to avoid it as well. A PC obsessed with their Mage Ascending sounds like a nightmare to play with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-22T14:56:57-08:00","id":1548713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1548710#post1548710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the issue I see here is that we do not know thoae characters paradigm and you are just assuming they have the vanilla hermetic and euthanatos paradigm, which is too shallow and might not be true.<br /> Other big issue is that those chars were created long before M20, so paradigm had not the structure M20 provides.<br /> <br /> I personally prefer to completely ignore MotA, because it is a 2e book AND the focus structure completely changed in M20. Also, there are no archspheres in M20 too.<br /> <br /> I don't know enough about those characters to analyze their paradigm, in fact, I'm not sure their ever explained their paradigms in detail. If they did, please tell me where.</div> </div> </div> </div>My understanding is that what M20 calls Paradigm and Practice were much more closely combined in earlier editions, and it was generally assumed that Mages from the same Tradition did share the same &quot;vanilla&quot; Paradigm. Hence why I felt fairly comfortable making that assumption, especially when talking about Archmages from Traditions with strongly defined philosophical principles. And as far as I know, those characters have never been written up in M20, so there is no available source material that would clarify what their Paradigm, in the M20 sense, would be.<br /> <br /> But again, my *point* is that they both illustrate the ways in which mastering the <b>tools</b> of magic does not confer the higher wisdom that is generally associated with the concept of Ascension. But reading what you've written below makes it pretty clear that we are not even close to being on the same wavelength on this subject...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1548710#post1548710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tbh, the &quot;Why&quot; isn't why you should do something (kill someone or do magick), but &quot;why&quot; can you do it. Paradigms (as in M20) should explain why mage can alter Reality and not &quot;why&quot; they should. And the &quot;why can&quot; will (and have to) be very well on par with the &quot;how&quot;.<br /> <br /> A chaote could answer those questions (in a very, VERY, simplified answer) like that:<br /> <br /> \u2022 How can you change reality? By achieving an altered state of consciousness that allows you to send your Will into the universe<br /> <br /> \u2022 Why can you change reality? &quot;As above, so below&quot;. What happena in the macroscomic level is reflected in the microcosmic level. There is a connection between the universe &quot;mind&quot; and the human mind, meaning that when on an altered state of consciousness (gnosis), the mage can directly &quot;connect&quot; to reality and change it.<br /> <br /> By practicing and studying more about gnosis and how magick works, the mage would also understand better about the connection with the universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's what you took from my &quot;How&quot; and &quot;Why&quot; distinction, then I feel like I wasted my time even trying to explain it.<br /> <br /> The way that you are describing it makes the distinction pointless, as far as I'm concerned. From my perspective, your version of &quot;How&quot; and &quot;Why&quot; both fit under the category of &quot;How&quot;. I can see why you have so much trouble with the concept of Ascension if that is the way you look at it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1548710#post1548710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems you are talking about open and closed paradigms? I believe chaos magick could be any of those. &quot;Everything is permitted&quot; could mean that you have no limits on your magick, but not that all paradigms are correct.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not. I'm talking about Ideals.<br /> <br /> The distinction between &quot;Open&quot; and &quot;Closed&quot; Paradigms is about &quot;How&quot; questions. It's about the extent to which a Paradigm can make the &quot;How&quot; of a different Paradigm fit around their own &quot;How&quot; framework, or if it is necessary to even do so.<br /> <br /> Ideals are about &quot;Why&quot;. What is the end goal? What is the ultimate purpose, the meaning of life? For me, the notion of many roads being able to lead to Ascension makes sense because there are many different possible Ideals that can be pursued or embodied. But that requires a person to be committed to some kind of Ideal, have some notion of perfection or spiritual evolution that they wish to pursue.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1548710#post1548710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not at all. I wouldn't consider omnipotence ascension. I was just wondering why one wouldn't ascend if seeking to increase spheres and arete. This thread has helped me understand a lot.<br /> <br /> I just think they should have explained a lot better in M20 instead of just saying increase in arete/spheres is bad for ascension.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of us seem to get by with the explanation provided in M20 just fine?<br /> <br /> They give Jesus and Buddha as examples, and most of us can extrapolate from that what kind of transformation that they are talking about, and have an idea of what that sort of thing would look like from the perspective of different Paradigms, even Paradigms wildly different from the ones you'd associate with those examples.<br /> <br /> It seems like you're having so much trouble with the idea of Ascension because you either don't get the concept of spiritual transcendence, or you just don't have any interest in it. As old-fashioned ceremonial magicians might put it, you're more interested in &quot;Low Magic&quot; than &quot;High Magic.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> may be correct that the best option for you would be to read through some of the Tradition books and get a better understanding of what Ascension looks like from their perspectives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-22T15:21:31-08:00","id":1548714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1548710#post1548710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally prefer to completely ignore MotA, because it is a 2e book AND the focus structure completely changed in M20. Also, there are no archspheres in M20 too.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not quite true. M20 p.68:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Rumor has it that levels of <b>Archmastery</b> exist for each Sphere, granting abstract powers that even gods might envy. In game terms, these world be the <i>EXTREMELY optional</i> Sphere ranks 6\u201310. Such powers are beyond almost every mage alive, take centuries to attain, and turn Chronicles into blasted wreckage. Groups that want to bring such powers into play can find them in the sourcebook <b>Masters of the Art</b>.</span></div> <br /> <br /> While it's a very tepid endorsement of MotA, it <i>is</i> still am endorsement: if you choose to involve Archspheres in your Chronicle, M20 points you to MotA for further details on how to do it. It uses language comparable in intensity to what it uses for &quot;don't play a Nephandus&quot;, albeit for different reasons; but it does ultimately end up pointing you to MotA for &quot;if you're going to, here's how&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-25-2025, 11:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-22T16:42:50-08:00","id":1548717,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11620_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11620\" data-vbnamecard=\"11620\">twig</a> I understand your feeling, it makes sense. In game, ascension tends to be forgotten or ignored. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25886\" data-vbnamecard=\"25886\">Kharnov</a> We do seem to be in different wave lengths. Would you care to explain your notion of &quot;Why&quot; with a Paradigm example? <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> I stand corrected, didn't remember that part of M20. Although I really dislike archspheres and wouldn't use them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-23T12:00:30-08:00","id":1548734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1548711#post1548711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To my taste, Ascension is a distraction and a trap. A character can get so focused on some ideal, impossible or otherwise, and it leads them down the wrong path.<br /> <br /> ....<br /> <br /> Basically unless I'm playing C20, I don't care about my PC 'ascending' as it were, and I would actively encourage my ST and fellow players to avoid it as well. A PC obsessed with their Mage Ascending sounds like a nightmare to play with.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:8px\">(I trimmed out the middle to shorten things because I'm not trying to address anything point-by-point.)</span><br /> <br /> To each their own, of course! I definitely agree with your take on justice-for-all versus a narrow focus on personal Ascension, at least when the character in question is supposed to be a &quot;good guy.&quot; It's why I like the idea of Mass Ascension as an ideal to pursue for everyone, and the notion of the &quot;Boddhisatva&quot; who holds back from achieving their own personal Ascension in order to try and help guide others along the path.\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1548717#post1548717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25886\" data-vbnamecard=\"25886\">Kharnov</a> We do seem to be in different wave lengths. Would you care to explain your notion of &quot;Why&quot; with a Paradigm example?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll elaborate a bit on three of the examples that I've already provided.<br /> <br /> First of all, let's talk about the &quot;traditional/default&quot; Hermetic Paradigm. Based on a wiki-overview of real-world Hermetic philosophy, the standard Hermetic Paradigm (in M20 terms) would probably be &quot;Bring Back the Golden Age,&quot; with some &quot;Divine Order, Earthly Chaos&quot; and &quot;Mechanistic Cosmos&quot; thrown in. Humans used to be perfect divine entities, given rulership over Creation by The One, but ended up somehow becoming trapped within it, becoming mundane creatures bound by the laws of material existence.<br /> <br /> The &quot;How&quot; of the Hermetic Focus, as described, is that humans still retain some of that divine spark, and they can draw upon ancient wisdom to figure out how to use that power to influence Creation. <br /> <br /> The &quot;Why&quot; of the Hermetic Focus is the ultimate end-goal that power is supposed to be used to achieve: transcending the imperfections of the material universe and become a perfect divine being once more.<br /> <br /> This process of becoming a perfect divine being is not just about becoming *powerful*, but also overcoming personal flaws and vices, as well as attachments to this mundane material existence. Magic can be helpful in this endeavour if you are using it in a way that helps you understand your limitations and overcome them, but not if you are just using it as a weapon in the pursuit of temporal power. And even if you intend to use your magical knowledge for the purposes of self-improvement, you have to engage with the wider material world to seek out that knowledge; Mages don't get to just pluck Sphere knowledge out of thin air. Thus every effort you make to seek out power and knowledge to help your Ascension comes with the risk of creating situations which drag you back into the muck of material existence, in the form of enemies you must fight or allies you must appease, whether you like it or not. Thus your pursuit of magical knowledge has to be careful weighed in terms of cost versus benefit towards your ultimate goal of spiritual enlightenment.<br /> <br /> This leads up back to Porthos. While he mastered the magical knowledge found within the Practices of the Order of Hermes, the &quot;How&quot;, he failed to use that knowledge to try and heal his wounded soul, resolving his guilt around the death of his family back in the Dark Ages, which would stand in the way of the spiritual perfection demanded by the &quot;Why&quot; of Hermetic philosophy. Despite his mostly-good intentions, he ultimately remained a flawed person, and thus could not achieve a Hermetic Ascension, becoming a perfect divine being once more.<br /> <br /> Let's talk about the Chakravanti/Euthanatos now. According to the M20 section on Paradigms, the typical Chakravanti position is something along the lines of &quot;Creation is Divine and Alive.&quot; They believe that their is a cosmic order (Destiny, Karma, etc.) that binds all of reality together, and gives a purpose to everything within it. Those who join the Chakravanti have a destined role to uphold and maintain this cosmic order, and they have access to great power in order to fulfill that function.<br /> <br /> The &quot;How&quot; of the Chakravanti is that they are permitted to draw upon the power of the gods in order to serve their destined role of keeping Fate on its proper course.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Why&quot; of the Chakravanti is using their powers to fulfill their role *correctly*, successfully keeping people on the course of their Dharma instead of impeding them or leading them astray. By fulfilling their own destined role, understanding their place in the cosmic order, they can eventually achieve Moksa, joining the ranks of the gods or becoming one with the universe.<br /> <br /> While the Chakravanti draw their power from the function that they are intended to serve, it is clear that they do not always do so successfully. Some members of the Tradition are criticized for being too willing to resort to the &quot;Good Death&quot; when other gentler methods might better serve the needs of Dharma. Magic itself may even be completely unnecessary in serving their function, if thoughtful advice is more than enough to steer an individual back onto the proper course. Thus pursuing greater magical knowledge only helps a Chakravanti in reaching Ascension inasmuch as it helps them to properly fulfill their destined purpose, and seeking power while ignoring their responsibilities would lead them away from Ascension, not towards it.<br /> <br /> Which brings us to Voormas. Voormas believed himself wise enough to judge the Wheel of Ages itself, thinking he had the right to try and force the fate of the entire universe to follow the path he had chosen. Underneath this, he also feared his own Karma, the consequences he was destined to face for the violence he embraced throughout his long life. He chose to reject his own fate, and rebel against the cosmic order that he was supposed to serve. Until he chose to return to the path of his Dharma, and accepts the Karma that he has brought upon himself, Voormas could not achieve Ascension as the Chakravanti understand it.<br /> <br /> You've argued before that either Porthos or Voormas may not follow the &quot;default&quot; Paradigm of their Traditions. But so what? They are both still clearly gripped by personal imperfections, lacking in philosophical or spiritual enlightenment, regardless of their formidable magic power. What path *could* they follow where those failings would not be a hindrance to their efforts at Ascension, unless Ascension is nothing more than &quot;being really good at doing magic&quot;?<br /> <br /> Let's wrap things up with the example that I gave for a Chaos Magician. Their Paradigm, of course, is that &quot;Everything is Chaos - You Only Think It Makes Sense.&quot; Unlike the Hermetic or the Chakravanti, they don't believe in a higher order, divine truth, whatever. There is no prior meaning of life or purpose for existence, no fate but what we make for ourselves.<br /> <br /> The &quot;How&quot; of Chaos Magic is that &quot;belief is a tool,&quot; that you can learn techniques to direct its power in order to manipulate the Chaos of the universe towards the results that you desire.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Why&quot; is a bit trickier in this case because &quot;Everything is Chaos&quot; rejects the notion of a universal meaning of life, divine plan, or &quot;higher&quot; form of existence. Unlike the previous two examples, it doesn't contain within it a predefined &quot;end&quot; that the Mage *should* be aimed towards achieving. This was why I think &quot;Transcend Your Limits&quot; is a good addition to a Chaos Mage's Paradigm, because it provides more direction in that regard than &quot;Everything is Chaos&quot; does on its own; the goal is to overcome your limitations, to self-actualize.<br /> <br /> You referred to my previous idea for the Chaos Mage version of Ascension as &quot;identity change,&quot; but I think that's a bit of an oversimplification. It's more about &quot;identity discovery,&quot; uncovering your &quot;True Will&quot; hidden beneath the beliefs that have been imposed upon you by your experiences, finding out what remains when all of the assumptions about who you &quot;are&quot; or &quot;should&quot; be have been stripped away. If &quot;Everything is Chaos,&quot; then so are You. You are One and You are Many, at the same time, contradiction be damned. A lot of this relies on the notion, supported by many of the originators of Chaos Magic philosophy, that we are all connected by the Kia/Collective Unconscious/Deep Mind, and the idea that we exist entirely as individuals, divided from everyone else, is just another belief, not an absolute truth. Our independent identity is just as much a construct as any other belief, and we should only adhere to it inasmuch as it proves itself useful. Eventually, all limitations are surpassed; not just on what can be done with magic, but on how the Chaos Mage understands themself and the infinity of Chaos, and Ascension is achieved.<br /> <br /> This is just one course that a Chaos Mage could try to follow towards Ascension, however. Compared to most other magical traditions, Chaos Magic is more pragmatic and less ideological. Different Chaos Mages can decide for themselves what &quot;liberation&quot; or &quot;self-actualization&quot; looks like. But, as I mentioned previously, I thoroughly reject the notion that Ascension is simply a matter of &quot;getting really good at magic,&quot; understanding the &quot;How&quot; of magic without ever embracing some notion of &quot;Why,&quot; having some notion of how You or Reality is made more perfect by the path that you have chosen. <br /> <br /> On a slightly separate note, it is worth mentioning that the writers chose to be vague about the nature of Ascension on purpose. They wanted it to be mysterious and ineffable. But also, they wanted to give Storytellers the room to decide for themselves what Ascension is supposed to mean at *their* table. If none of this really jives with you, there's no reason you can't handle it your own way as a Storyteller, or see if you can get the Storyteller on board with your interpretation if you are a player.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-23T17:55:44-08:00","id":1548742,"title":"","content":"On the topic of the writers not elucidating much about the nature of Ascension, I think that something relatively obvious that has been overlooked is that Mage was meant to model miracle-workers as a whole (with more standard occultists being covered by Sorcerer). I think that the vagueness was intentional, and from a pragmatic perspective, just good as a way to account for the different and often mutually exclusive models of liberation present in various religions. It seems like the developers tried to get that across by helping secular people grok mysticism more generally, but there is no need to necessarily reify what they said, particular when some models of liberation do necessarily involve omnipotence. We Are All (Gods) In Disguise stands as just one example of a paradigm from Book of Secrets that involves power, even if knowledge of the Spheres does not really assist one with enlightenment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-25T17:21:11-08:00","id":1548771,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25886\" data-vbnamecard=\"25886\">Kharnov</a> thank you very much for your detailed post.<br /> <br /> i just have one question that I'm not sure I know the answer.<br /> <br /> What is the rest of the questions of &quot;How&quot; and &quot;Why&quot;? &quot;How&quot; what? &quot;Why&quot; what? Exactly","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-26T09:03:39-08:00","id":1548787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1548771#post1548771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25886\" data-vbnamecard=\"25886\">Kharnov</a> thank you very much for your detailed post.<br /> <br /> i just have one question that I'm not sure I know the answer.<br /> <br /> What is the rest of the questions of &quot;How&quot; and &quot;Why&quot;? &quot;How&quot; what? &quot;Why&quot; what? Exactly</div> </div> </div> </div>It's &quot;How do they do Magic&quot; versus &quot;Why do they do Magic&quot;. At least in theory; in practice, plenty of Mages can utilize the &quot;How&quot; without necessarily being super committed to the &quot;Why&quot; associated with that magical theory. Chaos Magic is unusual in that it cares a lot less about the &quot;Why&quot; than most mystical frameworks.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-26T09:19:05-08:00","id":1548788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1548787#post1548787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's &quot;How do they do Magic&quot; versus &quot;Why do they do Magic&quot;. At least in theory; in practice, plenty of Mages can utilize the &quot;How&quot; without necessarily being super committed to the &quot;Why&quot; associated with that magical theory. Chaos Magic is unusual in that it cares a lot less about the &quot;Why&quot; than most mystical frameworks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do they do magick seems to be a very vague question, that would change from spell to spell and from mage to mage.<br /> <br /> If you mean why they do magick in a deeper way, then it would be as particular as a paradigm and would change from mage to mage.<br /> <br /> If you mean in a specific way (like why did you cast that fireball), then it would vary from spell to spell","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-26T15:29:27-08:00","id":1548797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1548788#post1548788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do they do magick seems to be a very vague question, that would change from spell to spell and from mage to mage.<br /> <br /> If you mean why they do magick in a deeper way, then it would be as particular as a paradigm and would change from mage to mage.<br /> <br /> If you mean in a specific way (like why did you cast that fireball), then it would vary from spell to spell</div> </div> </div> </div>So first of all, if you look at the EXTENSIVE examples that I provided in my previous post, it should be clear that I'm referring to the &quot;deeper way,&quot; at least when we're talking about the relationship between Paradigm and Ascension.<br /> <br /> Secondly, you're ignoring the fact that, while there is variation within them, each of the Traditions is defined by a broad philosophical framework that binds them together regardless of any particular differences that might arise from local/cultural perspectives or interpretations. That's what makes each of them a *Tradition* that can be bound together across the entire world.<br /> <br /> And third...<br /> <br /> Um... Yeah?<br /> <br /> The fact that the path to Ascension is a very personal thing that will vary even among Mages with similar Paradigm beliefs is a pretty good explanation for why there isn't a neat little list of &quot;10 Easy Steps That *Anyone* Can Follow To Achieve Ascension *Today*!&quot;<br /> <br /> If Ascension being vague and ineffable is a problem for you, then it's a problem for *you*, not the text. If it bothers you that much, then come up with your own concrete list of requirements like they give for Transcendence in Wraith. Again, half the reason it's written so vaguely is so that Storytellers can determine the meaning and requirements for themselves. The Roleplay Police will not bust down your door and throw you in Roleplay Jail for doing so.<br /> <br /> And, again, the other reason it's so vague is that we're talking about something that's supposed to be equivalent to achieving Nirvana in Buddhism, while *also* leaving room for it to fit into a dozen other radically different spiritual (or secular) worldviews.<br /> <br /> I can't really think of anything else to say that isn't just more of me repeating myself. If you're still just not getting it, I think I've just got to peace out and wish you good luck, at this point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-05T11:10:51-07:00","id":1560381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1548693#post1548693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Kitab_al-Alacir\" target=\"_blank\">Book of Ether</a> speaks of the Walls of Troy, a metaphor for reality. In this metaphor, everything is possible, even contradictory things. The Walls of Troy contain those things that have been accepted as possible, with everything outside the Walls being considered impossible. In this view, Ascension consists of tearing down the walls so that the Scientist truly accepts the infinite possibilities of reality. That's how an Etherite views Ascension: developing such a profound understanding of Ether Science that all things become possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>From my own reading of the Kitab al-Alacir passage found in the Sons of Ether Revised Tradition Book, I wouldn't say that the Kitab says that &quot;Walls of Troy&quot; (i.e. the Consensus) should be &quot;torn down&quot; per say (the passage even states that the &quot;Walls&quot; are necessary for normal human life, as without it we'd all go insane as our limited minds try and fail to grasp the whole of infinity) but more that they must be progressively &quot;expanded&quot;, until they eventually encompass all.<br /> <br /> And partially unrelated to the thread, but which M20 Paradigms (or combinations of them) would you say get closest to accurately reproducing this philosophy? M20 core book lists <i>A Mechanistic Cosmos</i>, <i>Tech Holds All Answers</i>, <i>Everything is Data</i>, <i>Everything\u2019s an Illusion</i> and <i>Might is Right</i> as options, and I\u2019d personally add <i>A Holographic Reality</i> from Book of Secrets as well. Opinions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28221,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28221-chronorebel","user":"ChronoRebel","date":". 06-05-2026, 03:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28221-chronorebel","name":"ChronoRebel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-05T12:09:23-07:00","id":1560383,"title":"","content":"A Mechanisistic view suggests that everything it's ruled by causality and there's no real free will. If anything accepting that contradictory truths can be possible depending on what's in and out of the Wall implies that cause it's of little use to determine an effect, and the cappability to choose which cause causes which effect.<br /> <br /> Tho, of course, some Etherites migth give the Paradigm a spin where it works - like saying the universe it's ruled by a god-machine that determines what's in and out of the Wall, and you're hacking it's designs<br /> <br /> Tech (science) holds all the answers it's definitely up there as a common belief. Everything it's an illusion, that can also be &quot;Everything it's Chaos&quot; definitely seems like it would have a place.<br /> <br /> Paradigms that can similarly capture the idea that reality holds infinite posibilities that you can capture trough science could have a go. Like a &quot;Migth Makes it Rigth&quot; Scientist following a kind of &quot;extreme formalism&quot; that values theories on how fascinating or elegant they are. And if facts don't seem to follow, well then clearly the facts are the problem (replace &quot;migth&quot; for &quot;elegance&quot;, if you may)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-05T12:09:57-07:00","id":1560384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChronoRebel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1560381#post1560381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From my own reading of the Kitab al-Alacir passage found in the Sons of Ether Revised Tradition Book, I wouldn't say that the Kitab says that &quot;Walls of Troy&quot; (i.e. the Consensus) should be &quot;torn down&quot; per say (the passage even states that the &quot;Walls&quot; are necessary for normal human life, as without it we'd all go insane as our limited minds try and fail to grasp the whole of infinity) but more that they must be progressively &quot;expanded&quot;, until they eventually encompass all.<br /> <br /> And partially unrelated to the thread, but which M20 Paradigms (or combinations of them) would you say get closest to accurately reproducing this philosophy? M20 core book lists <i>A Mechanistic Cosmos</i>, <i>Tech Holds All Answers</i>, <i>Everything is Data</i>, <i>Everything\u2019s an Illusion</i> and <i>Might is Right</i> as options, and I\u2019d personally add <i>A Holographic Reality</i> from Book of Secrets as well. Opinions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the fact that Consensus exists, I think the Might is Right depiction makes the most sense.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>&quot;The ones in power make the rules.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Though if we go by the theory of the 10th Sphere being the <b>Sphere of Judgement</b>, then you can say that ALL paradigms are true simultaneously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-06T00:31:03-07:00","id":1560403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1560383#post1560383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Mechanisistic view suggests that everything it's ruled by causality and there's no real free will. If anything accepting that contradictory truths can be possible depending on what's in and out of the Wall implies that cause it's of little use to determine an effect, and the cappability to choose which cause causes which effect.<br /> <br /> Tho, of course, some Etherites migth give the Paradigm a spin where it works - like saying the universe it's ruled by a god-machine that determines what's in and out of the Wall, and you're hacking it's designs<br /> <br /> Tech (science) holds all the answers it's definitely up there as a common belief. Everything it's an illusion, that can also be &quot;Everything it's Chaos&quot; definitely seems like it would have a place.<br /> <br /> Paradigms that can similarly capture the idea that reality holds infinite posibilities that you can capture trough science could have a go. Like a &quot;Migth Makes it Rigth&quot; Scientist following a kind of &quot;extreme formalism&quot; that values theories on how fascinating or elegant they are. And if facts don't seem to follow, well then clearly the facts are the problem (replace &quot;migth&quot; for &quot;elegance&quot;, if you may)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the flavor text for A Mechanistic Cosmos directly says that the Machine is meant to be tinkered with. And while I wasn\u2019t sure about Might is Right, your way of framing it makes sense.<br /> <br /> Personally, tho, I\u2019m partial to A Holographic Reality (from Book of Secrets). Here\u2019s the flavor text:<br /> <br /> \u00ab \u201cMatter\u201d is energy, shaped by our perceptions into the illusion of solidity. What we perceive as reality is in fact a holographic illusion of a greater Reality that exists at the edge of human awareness. Every element of this illusion is preserved in every other one, resulting in an infinite replication from which nothing is truly lost or destroyed. Although we catch glimpses of the truth in fleeting phenomena (d\u00e9j\u00e0 vu, precognition, telepathic contact, synchronicity, and other related \u201cimpossibilities\u201d), human existence as we know it demands limitations on what we can perceive. Awakening, however, removes the need for such binding and arbitrary limits. Ascension, then, involves opening one\u2019s self to the infinite truth and realizing that everything we \u201cknow\u201d is ultimately without substance, for All is One.<br /> A scientific perspective of the Everything\u2019s an Illusion and Creation\u2019s Divine and Alive paradigms, the holographic reality concept draws from quantum physics experiments within the last few decades. According to neurophysiologist Karl Pribram, the world as we know it is a \u201cworld of appearances,\u201d refined by human consciousness from a vast spectrum of interacting wave-forms. Although this world of appearances is \u201creal\u201d in most senses \u2013 inflicting boundaries upon what we can and cannot do within that world \u2013 it\u2019s essentially a projection of a boundless interplay of energies that we set into \u201cform\u201d through our consciousness. Within this paradigm, \u201cmagick\u201d (by any name) involves a recognition of, and an ability to manipulate, our world of appearances. Such feats, of course, are not supernaturalism, but science! Sure, ancient mystics may have first conceived of the truth, but it took science to prove its validity.<br /> Whether or not you consider this concept to be a paradigm in its own right, or simply a new spin on an old idea, is really up to the player and her Storyteller. Even so, the holographic reality concept \u2013 detailed in Michael Talbot\u2019s now-classic book The Holographic Universe \u2013 features a growing body of scientific research behind it. A character who embraces this paradigm (and who\u2019s familiar with that research) can spin dazzling webs of implacable techno-logic to support her work\u2026 and since the theory has at least one example of conclusive proof in the existence of the Digital Web, this paradigm enjoys surging popularity among twenty-first-century mages \u2013 mystic and technomancer alike! \u00bb","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28221,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28221-chronorebel","user":"ChronoRebel","date":". 06-06-2026, 04:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28221-chronorebel","name":"ChronoRebel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-28T00:17:27-07:00","id":1561069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games#post1547828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) If there is no objective Ascension, every mage might ascend differently and there is no definition of what Ascension really *is*. The books gives examples like jesus and Buddha, but also people who ascended through aggressiveness and negative doings. So, how does one knows that he has truly ascended? And would other mages acknowledge that? What if he thinks he ascended but didn't?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>One of the ToJ scenarios reveals that the <i>&quot;Tenth Sphere&quot;</i> is Judgement, and is associated with the mage's ability to shape reality based on their perception of it. In recognition of this, ALL forms of Ascension become true, and what exactly Ascension offers you is based upon what you believe it can offer.<br /> <br /> <br /> This is the idea that I personally choose to go with. Since we know that True Magic is the power to warp reality through the use of willpower and belief. I don't accept the idea of there being a singular, coherent form of Ascension, because the laws of magic can vary drastically, depending on who is the one using it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-03T16:27:12-07:00","id":1561261,"title":"","content":"When I first started playing I thought ascension was just some goal everyone picked for their player and did.<br /> <br /> So I decided to turn myself into a city, genius locii. Was going to live in the umbra and invite people in to help them awaken. Figure I could pull it off at campaign end if I could get everyone to help.<br /> <br /> Then no one else did anything with ascension and the St didn't do anything with characters ascending, I was confused and then some weeks or months in they told me in their world only like three people ever ascended outside of the oracles or whatever and I wondered what the point was. It's literally on the title. If VtM was called vampire the golcondaing I'd expect to do some Golconda stuff there to.<br /> <br /> Miffed about it.<br /> <br /> Still did turn into a city though.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-03T19:53:46-07:00","id":1561264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tjalei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1561261#post1561261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> and I wondered what the point was.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thinking about the concept, mostly.<br /> <br /> For all that's worth, your idea of Ascension's as valid as theirs. Also more to my licking.<br /> <br /> But above all else it's fodder for in-character conversation given that it has no rules or benefits attached. It's the justification for a lot of things, but in itself it's kind of whatever floats your boat.<br /> <br /> Mage is in the end a game of weaponized philosophy. Discussing Ascension is way more powerful than reaching it when people with the power to rewrite reality based on personal belief will take sides in wars based on the result of a debate, all the while your concept of Ascension will be one of the elements shaping your magic and the path your Avatar guides you to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-03T21:26:32-07:00","id":1561270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tjalei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1561261#post1561261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then no one else did anything with ascension and the St didn't do anything with characters ascending, I was confused and then some weeks or months in they told me in their world only like three people ever ascended outside of the oracles or whatever and I wondered what the point was. It's literally on the title. If VtM was called vampire the golcondaing I'd expect to do some Golconda stuff there to.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Ascension is pretty much an end game point for your character. It's the last thing they accomplish, before you retire their sheet and roll up a new one.<br /> <br /> Theoretically, your Ascension is supposed to be the point where you attain godlike power. Your mastery of magic and your understanding of how it works is so profound, that you don't even need a Foci anymore. You can just do your spells as effortlessly as breathing.<br /> <br /> <br /> Obviously, not the kind of character who sticks around as a PC. It would be like asking to play an Antedeluvian.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","user":"DarkKing","date":". 07-04-2026, 12:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-03T22:00:33-07:00","id":1561274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1561270#post1561270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, Ascension is pretty much an end game point for your character. It's the last thing they accomplish, before you retire their sheet and roll up a new one.<br /> <br /> Theoretically, your Ascension is supposed to be the point where you attain godlike power. Your mastery of magic and your understanding of how it works is so profound, that you don't even need a Foci anymore. You can just do your spells as effortlessly as breathing.<br /> <br /> <br /> Obviously, not the kind of character who sticks around as a PC. It would be like asking to play an Antedeluvian.</div> </div> </div> </div>The books don't actually say any of those things, and the text in some actually gives the idea that keeping playing after Ascension is perfectly ok.<br /> <br /> Abandoning foci is Arete, and it's said it isn't the same as Ascension. Godlike power is the whole point of the game, but beyond that the only time they talked about even more power seriously was on Archmastery, and that book literally says you give up on Ascension in the process.<br /> <br /> So... Ascension basically gives you bragging rights. Which is possibly the most coveted prize among Mages, but kind of ends there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-03T22:22:22-07:00","id":1561277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1561274#post1561274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The books don't actually say any of those things, and the text in some actually gives the idea that keeping playing after Ascension is perfectly ok.<br /> <br /> Abandoning foci is Arete, and it's said it isn't the same as Ascension. Godlike power is the whole point of the game, but beyond that the only time they talked about even more power seriously was on Archmastery, and that book literally says you give up on Ascension in the process.<br /> <br /> So... Ascension basically gives you bragging rights. Which is possibly the most coveted prize among Mages, but kind of ends there.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I got a different impression, by reading what the traditionalists are trying to achieve, or what they believe in.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Order of Hermes</b> - believe that through their codified application of magic, they can achieve a level of status where they stand as God's equals.<br /> <br /> <b>Akashics</b> - seek to escape the cycle of reincarnation and achieve a state of oneness with the universe around them.<br /> <br /> <b>Verbena</b> - see themselves as being a microcosm of the universe, and ultimately seek to evolve into what they consider to be the perfect version of themselves.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-03T23:01:39-07:00","id":1561279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1561277#post1561277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I got a different impression, by reading what the traditionalists are trying to achieve, or what they believe in.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's their party lines about Ascension. The word has several possible meanings in the game. Those beliefs have nothing to do with personal Ascension, which is what we talk about when we say a Mage achieved Ascension.<br /> <br /> Basically those Tradition lines are just blurb to help get their philosophies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-04T00:12:16-07:00","id":1561283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1561279#post1561279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's their party lines about Ascension. The word has several possible meanings in the game. Those beliefs have nothing to do with personal Ascension, which is what we talk about when we say a Mage achieved Ascension.<br /> <br /> Basically those Tradition lines are just blurb to help get their philosophies.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my opinion, I think focusing on personal Ascension is the way to go.<br /> <br /> Mass Ascension is pretty much a lost cause at this point for Traditionalists. Either because the Technocrats are winning, or the Nephandi are.<br /> <br /> Might as well focus on cash your chips early and start over in a new universe, parallel to this one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-04T19:34:21-07:00","id":1561328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games#post1547828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to know how ascension affects your games and players actions, if it ever do.<br /> I have some issues with ascension as written in M20 for a few reasons:<br /> <br /> 1) Ascension is described as a very, very rare state (&quot;more of an ideal than an accomplishment&quot; M20 p.23) by which mages often disagree what it means. So, mages aren't sure what it is nor how to achieve it. Why would a mage seek something that he doesn't know if its real and you dont know what is/how to seek? Why would one actively seek/want Ascension?<br /> <br /> 2) If there is no objective Ascension, every mage might ascend differently and there is no definition of what Ascension really *is*. The books gives examples like jesus and Buddha, but also people who ascended through aggressiveness and negative doings. So, how does one knows that he has truly ascended? And would other mages acknowledge that? What if he thinks he ascended but didn't?<br /> <br /> 3)My main issue: M20 describes ascension in p.370 as<br /> <br /> &quot;As The Book of Mirrors points out (pps. 60-61), Ascension is not hitting Arete 10 or maxing out all your Spheres. It\u2019s not about power but about the transcendence of the need for power. Mere power, in Mage, is a trap. The more a mage pursues it, the further she gets from ultimate Ascension. Even if her Path is all about power (see the Might is Right paradigm in Chapter Ten), that person must still grow beyond the need to acquire power.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Since ascension depends on paradigm *and isn't strictly related to higher/good moral and virtue*, why does seeking power gets in the way of ascending? Why could one ascend by going on a killing spree but not seeking power?<br /> More so, if ascension is directly related to magickal knowledge (stated in raw), why increasing Arete/Spheres would be bad for ascending?<br /> <br /> In conclusion, players are always seeking more xp, power, Arete, etc. How can you play the game *and* seek ascension when growing in power is bad for ascension?<br /> How do you reconcile the seek of power that every game has and ascension?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've read throughout this thread, and I think you're falling into a bit of a trap here. Saying &quot;Ascension is not hitting Arete 10&quot; is not the same thing as saying &quot;increasing Arete is not part of the path to Ascension.&quot; It's more akin, in my interpretation, to saying &quot;a taco is not just a tortilla.&quot; The flowering of Enoch into Metatron, or the luminal phase that Elijah exists in in Jewish folklore between wandering the Earth as an anonymous old man and entering Heaven as Sandalphon, or Lilith becoming a Pure One in Bahari lore could all be taken as Ascension, or in the case of Elijah, demonstrating Ascension as a process - his Ascension isn't finished, so he wanders in that liminal state.<br /> <br /> To the discussions about leaving practice behind vs leaving instruments behind, according to Dante's write-up in Lore of the Traditions, he basically doesn't need practice at all anymore, but he does favor Reality Hacking out of habit. As Dante is the only Oracle of the modern age, I think he's a good example to go by.<br /> <br /> It's possible that true Ascension requires Arete 10, but not only Arete 10. Perhaps you must take the Oracle Path described in MotA as well.<br /> <br /> Edit: I do think, based on the Times of Judgement Ascension book, Ascension does require some amount of moral and spiritual perfection. I'm aware that that might contradict that particular M20 passage, or even Lilith's Ascension, but I never claimed to have all the pieces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26432-jagnestormskull","name":"JagneStormskull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26432_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-05T08:13:07-07:00","id":1561345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1547888#post1547888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The final word in the book comes in a box talking about &quot;Ascension in the Context of Salvation&quot;. It talks a bit about Golconda, Transcendence, and &quot;even changelings have their own enlightened states through which they attain the one strength to take on the world.&quot; (As an aside, I notice that werewolves aren't included in this discussion. Strange.) It contrasts Ascension with these in that they involve accepting or balancing your dark side, whereas Ascension involves purifying it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did ask Werewolf players about whether or not there is a Garou Golconda (or Transcendence, or Ascension, or however the Changeling version is spelled), and the most common responses fell into a couple of categories:<br /> 1) A Garou's purpose is pre-defined, and they cannot escape it (which, in the lore, is backed by a Stargazer belief that Garou can't attain Nirvana because it would be abandoning their post).<br /> 2) Unlike vampires, Garou are awesome and have no weaknesses! (You know, ignoring silver, Thrall of the Wyrm, or mortality)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26432-jagnestormskull","name":"JagneStormskull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26432_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-05T17:22:01-07:00","id":1561361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JagneStormskull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1561345#post1561345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I did ask Werewolf players about whether or not there is a Garou Golconda (or Transcendence, or Ascension, or however the Changeling version is spelled), and the most common responses fell into a couple of categories:<br /> 1) A Garou's purpose is pre-defined, and they cannot escape it (which, in the lore, is backed by a Stargazer belief that Garou can't attain Nirvana because it would be abandoning their post).<br /> 2) Unlike vampires, Garou are awesome and have no weaknesses! (You know, ignoring silver, Thrall of the Wyrm, or mortality)</div> </div> </div> </div>They're both kinda correct.<br /> <br /> Shapechangers are custom-built half-spirit entities. They have no human soul, no internal spiritual clash, and no mystery about their final destiny. Their Rage is part of their nature and a feature to use despite drawbacks, not a curse.<br /> <br /> Now, there is something to strive for, but not as much as a transcendence: to join the venerable Ancestors. Upon death a Garou becomes spirit and travels to their Tribe's Ancestor Lands in the Middle Umbra. But great heroes not only get to be more powerful spirits, they get to be revered by the living and have some influence in the material through them.<br /> <br /> But that's it. The problems that plague them is of another nature and more about society. You see: Vampires, Mages and Changelings get to find inner accomplishment despite their social environment, all by themselves. The great challenge is personal.<br /> <br /> Garou are challenged with a society that's so overtaken with its own quibbles and prejudices that they're wasting effort at best and worsening the situation at worse. They don't get the luxury to ignore the toxic environment.<br /> <br /> While I'm here: the Changeling counterpart is called S\u00edoch\u00e1in (Irish for &quot;peace&quot;), and are said to have found the perfect balance between Glamour and Banality. They become ageless and possibly harder or impossible to kill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-06T11:05:30-07:00","id":1561389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1561361#post1561361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They're both kinda correct.<br /> <br /> Shapechangers are custom-built half-spirit entities. They have no human soul, no internal spiritual clash, and no mystery about their final destiny. Their Rage is part of their nature and a feature to use despite drawbacks, not a curse.<br /> <br /> Now, there is something to strive for, but not as much as a transcendence: to join the venerable Ancestors. Upon death a Garou becomes spirit and travels to their Tribe's Ancestor Lands in the Middle Umbra. But great heroes not only get to be more powerful spirits, they get to be revered by the living and have some influence in the material through them.<br /> <br /> But that's it. The problems that plague them is of another nature and more about society. You see: Vampires, Mages and Changelings get to find inner accomplishment despite their social environment, all by themselves. The great challenge is personal.<br /> <br /> Garou are challenged with a society that's so overtaken with its own quibbles and prejudices that they're wasting effort at best and worsening the situation at worse. They don't get the luxury to ignore the toxic environment.<br /> <br /> While I'm here: the Changeling counterpart is called S\u00edoch\u00e1in (Irish for &quot;peace&quot;), and are said to have found the perfect balance between Glamour and Banality. They become ageless and possibly harder or impossible to kill.</div> </div> </div> </div>That last one is why I mentioned mortality as a weakness of the Garou. I also think that the Garou being very religious about Rage (and its final form, Thrall of the Wyrm) is similar to the Sabbat's Path of the Beast being centered on the idea that the Beast is not a curse - them saying it doesn't actually make it true. The Thrall of the Wyrm is proof that the Garou's blessed Rage is not always what it's cracked up to be. <br /> <br /> Garou are both wolf and man. To reconcile these contradictions is an interesting story to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26432-jagnestormskull","name":"JagneStormskull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26432_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-06T22:32:14-07:00","id":1561412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JagneStormskull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1561389#post1561389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Thrall of the Wyrm is proof that the Garou's blessed Rage is not always what it's cracked up to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not lost on them. The drawbacks are strong and powerful.<br /> <br /> But it's literally a resource they can use for extra actions and as Gift fuel. It's demonstrably a strength, and still natural for them, not an intrusion.<br /> <br /> A Garou that gets rid of Rage looses the Wolf, becoming little more than a Kinfolk. So there's really no notion of &quot;transcending the Rage&quot; for them.<br /> <br /> So yeah, while I'd say they're the <i>idea</i> of a wolf, rather than an actual wolf, they're both human and beast. But that's the point: to find your way to live with that rather to transcend to become something else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-07T12:23:35-07:00","id":1561425,"title":"","content":"<br /> .<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> =monteparnasBut it's literally a resource they can use for extra actions and as Gift fuel. It's demonstrably a strength, and still natural for them, not an intrusion </div> </div> </div>Yeah, <br /> <br /> Also, I would argue that if there's any kind of &quot;higher spiritual state&quot; the Fera could strive to get, it's restoring balance between the three forces that make up nature. Getting rid of the Wyrm's influence ain't that.<br /> <br /> Solving it internaly would be contrary to the spirit of the game about caring about the world.<br /> <br /> But if they did managed to re-balance the Wyrm, that would likely lead to a healthier Rage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-20T05:25:11-07:00","id":1561968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547828-ascension-in-games?p=1547879#post1547879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Might Makes Right</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Thus Spoke Zarathustra, the first Ascended and the prophet of the way of the Ubermensch.<br /> <br /> For the &quot;Will to Power&quot; is the ultimate nature of reality, for all living beings naturally feel the need to input their will into the world.<br /> <br /> But the ultimate expression of will to power, is the expression of will to power over oneself. To will the power one's environment is a valid path, but the will to power over oneself is the final achievement for any living beings.&quot;<br /> <br /> Nietzschean ideas fit perfectly in here, and in fact, I would say that this is the best designed Paradigm that exists due to it; also, the path towards Ascension through that particular Paradigm is already laid out on Nietzsche's ideas from &quot;Thus Spoke Zarathustra&quot; and also on his other book &quot;Beyond Good and Evil&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29126-phooku","name":"Phooku","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}